w.painter is ScanlinesPainter,\n504:         ),\n505:         findsNothing,\n506:       );\n507:       expect(find.text('CAM-01 · hallway'), findsOneWidget);\n508:       expect(tester.takeException(), isNull);\n509:     });\n510: \n511:     testWidgets('settings label overrides win over manifest clip labels',\n512:         (WidgetTester tester) async {\n513:       // Precedence composition on one wall: the manifest carries a clip\n514:       // label for CAM-01 AND settings carry an override for the same\n515:       // camera — settings win. CAM-03 keeps its manifest label, CAM-02\n516:       // and CAM-04 keep slot defaults.\n517:       final HauntedSurveillancePlugin plugin = HauntedSurveillancePlugin(\n518:         disableEffects: true,\n519:         manifest: _manifest(\n520:           labels: const <String, String?>{\n521:             'CAM-01': 'Manifest Door',\n522:             'CAM-03': 'Manifest Basement',\n523:           },\n524:         ),\n525:         tileBuilder: _fakeSurface,\n526:       );\n527:       final ChannelContext ctx = ChannelContext(\n528:         partyId: PartyId('party-1'),\n529:         playbackHandle: _FakeHandle(),\n530:         settings: const ChannelSettings(<String, Object?>{\n531:           'labels': <String, String>{'CAM-01': 'PORCH · settings'},\n532:         }),\n533:       );\n534:       await tester.pumpWidget(MaterialApp(home: plugin.build(ctx)));\n535:       await tester.pumpAndSettle();\n536: \n537:       expect(find.text('PORCH · settings'), findsOneWidget);\n538:       expect(find.text('Manifest Door'), findsNothing);\n539:       expect(find.text('Manifest Basement'), findsOneWidget);\n540:       expect(find.text('CAM-02 · kitchen'), findsOneWidget);\n541:       expect(find.text('CAM-04 · storage room'), findsOneWidget);\n542:       expect(tester.takeException(), isNull);\n543:     });\n544: \n545:     test('cctvLabelOverridesFromSettings filters non-Map/non-string shapes',\n546:         () {\n547:       // No `labels` key at all.\n548:       expect(\n549:         cctvLabelOverridesFromSettings(const ChannelSettings()),\n550:         isEmpty,\n551:       );\n552:       // Non-Map value is ignored, not thrown on.\n553:       expect(\n554:         cctvLabelOverridesFromSettings(\n555:           const ChannelSettings(<String, Object?>{'labels': 'PORCH'}),\n556:         ),\n557:         isEmpty,\n558:       );\n559:       // Non-string keys/values are dropped; only String->String survives.\n560:       expect(\n561:         cctvLabelOverridesFromSettings(\n562:           const ChannelSettings(<String, Object?>{\n563:             'labels': <Object?, Object?>{\n564:               'CAM-01': 'Porch',\n565:               'CAM-02': 42,\n566:               'CAM-03': null,\n567:               7: 'Attic',\n568:             },\n569:           }),\n570:         ),\n571:         <String, String>{'CAM-01': 'Porch'},\n572:       );\n573:     });\n574:   });\n575: \n576:   group('port direction (D-08)', () {\n577:     // Finding D-08: channels must be able to consume the control-plane ports\n578:     // without importing `infra_*`. These two tests keep that true from the\n579:     // consumer side: one walks the real import graph, the other compiles and\n580:     // runs fakes implemented purely against `channel_api`.\n581:     test('lib graph of this channel imports no infra_* package', () {\n582:       final Set<String> visitedPackages = <String>{};\n583:       final List<File> sources = _transitiveLibSources(\n584:         Directory.current,\n585:         visitedPackages,\n586:       );\n587:       expect(\n588:         visitedPackages,\n589:         containsAll(<String>['channel_cctv', 'channel_api']),\n590:         reason: 'walk must actually reach the contracts package',\n591:       );\n592:       final List<String> offenders = <String>[\n593:         for (final File f in sources)\n594:           if (f.readAsStringSync().contains('package:infra_')) f.path,\n595:       ];\n596:       expect(\n597:         offenders,\n598:         isEmpty,\n599:         reason: 'channels must not import infra_* (finding D-08)',\n600:       );\n601:     });\n602: \n603:     test('ports are implementable from channel_api alone', () async {\n604:       final _ContractOnlyManifestSource source = _ContractOnlyManifestSource(\n605:         _manifest(),\n606:       );\n607:       final ManifestSource<PlaybackManifest> port = source;\n608:       final List<PlaybackManifest> seen = await port\n609:           .watchCurrent(partyId: 'party-1', channelId: hauntedSurveillanceChannelId)\n610:           .toList();\n611:       expect(seen, hasLength(1));\n612:       expect(seen.single.channelId, hauntedSurveillanceChannelId);\n613: \n614:       final SettingsPort settings = _ContractOnlySettings();\n615:       await settings.setString(\n616:         partyId: PartyId('party-1'),\n617:         key: 'label.cam-01',\n618:         value: 'Front Door',\n619:       );\n620:       expect(\n621:         await settings.getString(\n622:           partyId: PartyId('party-1'),\n623:           key: 'label.cam-01',\n624:         ),\n625:         'Front Door',\n626:       );\n627:     });\n628:   });\n629: }\n630: \n631: \n632: /// Collects the `lib/` sources of [packageRoot] and, transitively, of every\n633: /// sibling path package reachable through `package:<name>/<path>` imports.\n634: ///\n635: /// Only local siblings (`<packages>/<name>/lib/*.dart`) are followed, so SDK\n636: /// and pub-cache packages terminate the walk. Names are recorded in\n637: /// [visited] so the caller can assert the graph was not vacuous.\n638: List<File> _transitiveLibSources(Directory packageRoot, Set<String> visited) {\n639:   final List<File> collected = <File>[];\n640:   final List<(String, Directory)> queue = <(String, Directory)>[\n641:     (_packageNameOf(packageRoot), packageRoot),\n642:   ];\n643:   while (queue.isNotEmpty) {\n644:     final (String name, Directory root) = queue.removeLast();\n645:     if (!visited.add(name)) {\n646:       continue;\n647:     }\n648:     final Directory lib = Directory('${root.path}/lib');\n649:     if (!lib.existsSync()) {\n650:       continue;\n651:     }\n652:     for (final File file in lib.listSync(recursive: true).whereType<File>()) {\n653:       if (!file.path.endsWith('.dart')) {\n654:         continue;\n655:       }\n656:       collected.add(file);\n657:       for (final String uri in _packageUrisOf(file.readAsStringSync())) {\n658:         final String target = uri.split('/').first;\n659:         final Directory sibling = Directory('${packageRoot.parent.path}/$target');\n660:         if (sibling.existsSync()) {\n661:           queue.add((target, sibling));\n662:         }\n663:       }\n664:     }\n665:   }\n666:   return collected;\n667: }\n668: \n669: /// Package name of [root], read from its `pubspec.yaml` name line.\n670: String _packageNameOf(Directory root) {\n671:   final File pubspec = File('${root.path}/pubspec.yaml');\n672:   for (final String line in pubspec.readAsLinesSync()) {\n673:     if (line.startsWith('name:')) {\n674:       return line.substring('name:'.length).trim();\n675:     }\n676:   }\n677:   return root.uri.pathSegments.where((String s) => s.isNotEmpty).last;\n678: }\n679: \n680: /// `package:<name>/<path>` URIs referenced by [source].\n681: Iterable<String> _packageUrisOf(String source) sync* {\n682:   for (final RegExpMatch match\n683:       in RegExp(r'package:([a-z0-9_]+/[A-Za-z0-9_./]+)')\n684:           .allMatches(source)) {\n685:     yield match.group(1)!;\n686:   }\n687: }\n688: \n689: /// Manifest source bound to `PlaybackManifest` using only the contracts port.\n690: final class _ContractOnlyManifestSource\n691:     implements ManifestSource<PlaybackManifest> {\n692:   _ContractOnlyManifestSource(this.manifest);\n693: \n694:   final PlaybackManifest manifest;\n695: \n696:   @override\n697:   Stream<PlaybackManifest> watchCurrent({\n698:     required String partyId,\n699:     required String channelId,\n700:   }) async* {\n701:     yield manifest;\n702:   }\n703: }\n704: \n705: /// Settings store written against the contracts port; no infra adapter used.\n706: final class _ContractOnlySettings implements SettingsPort {\n707:   final Map<String, String> _values = <String, String>{};\n708: \n709:   @override\n710:   Future<String?> getString({\n711:     required PartyId partyId,\n712:     required String key,\n713:   }) async => _values['${partyId.value}/$key'];\n714: \n715:   @override\n716:   Future<void> setString({\n717:     required PartyId partyId,\n718:     required String key,\n719:     required String value,\n720:   }) async {\n721:     _values['${partyId.value}/$key'] = value;\n722:   }\n723: \n724:   @override\n725:   Future<bool?> getBool({\n726:     required PartyId partyId,\n727:     required String key,\n728:   }) async => _values['${partyId.value}/$key'] == 'true';\n729: \n730:   @override\n731:   Future<void> setBool({\n732:     required PartyId partyId,\n733:     required String key,\n734:     required bool value,\n735:   }) async {\n736:     _values['${partyId.value}/$key'] = '$value';\n737:   }\n738: }\n739: \n740: Widget _fakeSurface(\n741:   BuildContext context,\n742:   int index,\n743:   String label,\n744:   String cameraId,\n745: ) =>\n746:     Container(color: Colors.black, key: Key('surface-$cameraId'));\n747: \n748: Widget _throwingSurface(\n749:   BuildContext context,\n750:   int index,\n751:   String label,\n752:   String cameraId,\n753: ) {\n754:   throw StateError('no decoder in tests');\n755: }\n756: \n757: /// Inline stand-in for a sibling channel's descriptor id contract.\n758: final class _SiblingStubPlugin implements ChannelPlugin {\n759:   const _SiblingStubPlugin();\n760: \n761:   @override\n762:   ChannelDescriptor get descriptor => const ChannelDescriptor(\n763:         id: 'retro_horror',\n764:         title: 'Retro Horror',\n765:         version: 1,\n766:       );\n767: \n768:   @override\n769:   Widget build(ChannelContext context) => const SizedBox.shrink();\n770: }","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-2/packages/channel_cctv/test/channel_cctv_test.dart, lines 1-770\n1: import 'dart:io';\n2: \n3: import 'package:channel_api/channel_api.dart';\n4: import 'package:channel_cctv/channel_cctv.dart';\n5: import 'package:core_effects/core_effects.dart';\n6: import 'package:core_foundation/core_foundation.dart';\n7: import 'package:core_playlist/core_playlist.dart';\n8: import 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n9: import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';\n10: \n11: final class _FakeHandle implements PlaybackHandle {\n12:   bool prepared = false;\n13: \n14:   @override\n15:   Future<void> prepare() async {\n16:     prepared = true;\n17:   }\n18: \n19:   @override\n20:   Future<void> activate() async {}\n21: }\n22: \n23: final class _FailingHandle implements PlaybackHandle {\n24:   @override\n25:   Future<void> prepare() async => throw StateError('coordinator offline');\n26: \n27:   @override\n28:   Future<void> activate() async {}\n29: }\n30: \n31: final class _FakeClock implements Clock {\n32:   _FakeClock(this.current);\n33: \n34:   DateTime current;\n35: \n36:   @override\n37:   DateTime now() => current;\n38: }\n39: \n40: /// Sixty-four lowercase hex chars (valid sha256 shape for fixtures).\n41: const String _sha = 'aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa';\n42: \n43: PlaybackManifest _manifest({\n44:   OverlaySettings overlay = const OverlaySettings(),\n45:   Map<String, String?> labels = const <String, String?>{},\n46:   bool reverseClipOrder = false,\n47: }) {\n48:   final List<ClipDescriptor> clips = <ClipDescriptor>[\n49:     for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++)\n50:       ClipDescriptor(\n51:         id: 'clip-0$i',\n52:         cameraId: 'CAM-0${i + 1}',\n53:         storageObjectId: 'obj-0$i',\n54:         sha256: _sha,\n55:         sizeBytes: 1024,\n56:         duration: const Duration(seconds: 4),\n57:         mimeType: 'video/mp4',\n58:         label: labels['CAM-0${i + 1}'],\n59:       ),\n60:   ];\n61:   return PlaybackManifest(\n62:     partyId: 'party-1',\n63:     channelId: hauntedSurveillanceChannelId,\n64:     version: 3,\n65:     publishedAt: DateTime.utc(2026, 10, 31, 20),\n66:     clips: reverseClipOrder ? clips.reversed.toList() : clips,\n67:     overlay: overlay,\n68:   );\n69: }\n70: \n71: void main() {\n72:   group('tileFor', () {\n73:     test('maps slots 0..3 to CAM-01..04 with rooms', () {\n74:       expect(tileFor(0), (label: 'CAM-01 · hallway', cameraId: 'CAM-01'));\n75:       expect(tileFor(1), (label: 'CAM-02 · kitchen', cameraId: 'CAM-02'));\n76:       expect(tileFor(2), (label: 'CAM-03 · staircase', cameraId: 'CAM-03'));\n77:       expect(\n78:           tileFor(3), (label: 'CAM-04 · storage room', cameraId: 'CAM-04'));\n79:     });\n80: \n81:     test('rejects out-of-range slots', () {\n82:       expect(() => tileFor(-1), throwsRangeError);\n83:       expect(() => tileFor(4), throwsRangeError);\n84:     });\n85: \n86:     test('slot list and labels derive from core_playlist cctvSlots', () {\n87:       expect(cctvCameraIds, cctvSlots.map((CctvSlot s) => s.id).toList());\n88:       expect(cctvRooms, cctvSlots.map((CctvSlot s) => s.room).toList());\n89:       expect(() => cctvCameraIds.add('CAM-99'), throwsUnsupportedError);\n90:       expect(() => cctvRooms.add('attic'), throwsUnsupportedError);\n91:     });\n92: \n93:     test('a custom label overrides the slot default, blank keeps it', () {\n94:       expect(\n95:         tileFor(0, label: 'Front Door'),\n96:         (label: 'Front Door', cameraId: 'CAM-01'),\n97:       );\n98:       expect(\n99:         tileFor(0, label: '   '),\n100:         (label: cctvSlots[0].defaultLabel, cameraId: 'CAM-01'),\n101:       );\n102:       expect(\n103:         tileFor(0),\n104:         (label: cctvSlots[0].defaultLabel, cameraId: 'CAM-01'),\n105:       );\n106:     });\n107: \n108:     test('tileForCamera places by camera identity, not index', () {\n109:       expect(\n110:         tileForCamera('CAM-03', label: 'Stairs'),\n111:         (label: 'Stairs', cameraId: 'CAM-03'),\n112:       );\n113:       expect(() => tileForCamera('CAM-09'), throwsArgumentError);\n114:     });\n115: \n116:     test('tileForClip resolves config labels, else slot defaults', () {\n117:       ClipDescriptor clip(String cameraId, {String? label}) => ClipDescriptor(\n118:         id: 'clip-$cameraId',\n119:         cameraId: cameraId,\n120:         storageObjectId: 'obj-$cameraId',\n121:         sha256: _sha,\n122:         sizeBytes: 1024,\n123:         duration: const Duration(seconds: 4),\n124:         mimeType: 'video/mp4',\n125:         label: label,\n126:       );\n127:       expect(\n128:         tileForClip(clip('CAM-02', label: 'Kitchen Cam')),\n129:         (label: 'Kitchen Cam', cameraId: 'CAM-02'),\n130:       );\n131:       expect(\n132:         tileForClip(clip('CAM-04')),\n133:         (label: cctvSlots[3].defaultLabel, cameraId: 'CAM-04'),\n134:       );\n135:     });\n136:   });\n137: \n138:   group('HauntedSurveillancePlugin', () {\n139:     test('descriptor is valid with wall capabilities', () {\n140:       const ChannelPlugin plugin = HauntedSurveillancePlugin();\n141:       expect(plugin.descriptor.id, hauntedSurveillanceChannelId);\n142:       expect(plugin.descriptor.title, 'Haunted Surveillance');\n143:       expect(plugin.descriptor.version, greaterThan(0));\n144:       expect(plugin.descriptor.capabilities.videoPlayback, isTrue);\n145:       expect(plugin.descriptor.capabilities.effects, isTrue);\n146:       expect(plugin.descriptor.capabilities.timedEvents, isTrue);\n147:     });\n148: \n149:     test('descriptor round-trips through json', () {\n150:       const ChannelPlugin plugin = HauntedSurveillancePlugin();\n151:       final ChannelDescriptor back =\n152:           ChannelDescriptor.fromJson(plugin.descriptor.toJson());\n153:       expect(back.id, hauntedSurveillanceChannelId);\n154:       expect(back.capabilities, plugin.descriptor.capabilities);\n155:     });\n156: \n157:     test('is registry-compatible alongside sibling channels', () {\n158:       // Inline registry shape (no kernel_app import needed); the sibling\n159:       // stub stands in for RetroHorrorPlugin's descriptor id contract.\n160:       final Map<String, ChannelPlugin> registry = <String, ChannelPlugin>{\n161:         for (final ChannelPlugin p in <ChannelPlugin>[\n162:           const HauntedSurveillancePlugin(),\n163:           const _SiblingStubPlugin(),\n164:         ])\n165:           p.descriptor.id: p,\n166:       };\n167:       expect(registry['haunted_surveillance'],\n168:           isA<HauntedSurveillancePlugin>());\n169:       expect(registry['retro_horror'], isA<_SiblingStubPlugin>());\n170:     });\n171: \n172:     testWidgets('boots the wall with a fake coordinator',\n173:         (WidgetTester tester) async {\n174:       final _FakeHandle handle = _FakeHandle();\n175:       final HauntedSurveillancePlugin plugin = HauntedSurveillancePlugin(\n176:         disableEffects: true,\n177:         tileBuilder: _fakeSurface,\n178:         clock: _FakeClock(DateTime(2026, 10, 31, 20)),\n179:       );\n180:       final ChannelContext ctx = ChannelContext(\n181:         partyId: PartyId('party-1'),\n182:         playbackHandle: handle,\n183:       );\n184:       await tester.pumpWidget(MaterialApp(home: plugin.build(ctx)));\n185:       await tester.pumpAndSettle();\n186:       expect(handle.prepared, isTrue);\n187:       expect(find.text('CAM-01 · hallway'), findsOneWidget);\n188:       expect(find.text('CAM-02 · kitchen'), findsOneWidget);\n189:       expect(find.text('CAM-03 · staircase'), findsOneWidget);\n190:       expect(find.text('CAM-04 · storage room'), findsOneWidget);\n191:       expect(find.text('REC'), findsWidgets);\n192:       expect(find.text('20:00:00'), findsNWidgets(4));\n193:       expect(find.text('SIGNAL LOST'), findsNothing);\n194:     });\n195: \n196:     testWidgets('manifest without labels falls back to core_playlist defaults',\n197:         (WidgetTester tester) async {\n198:       // Manifest clips carry no `label`: wall labels must resolve to the\n199:       // canonical slot defaults from core_playlist, never to clip ids.\n200:       final _FakeHandle handle = _FakeHandle();\n201:       final HauntedSurveillancePlugin plugin = HauntedSurveillancePlugin(\n202:         disableEffects: true,\n203:         manifest: _manifest(),\n204:         tileBuilder: _fakeSurface,\n205:       );\n206:       final ChannelContext ctx = ChannelContext(\n207:         partyId: PartyId('party-1'),\n208:         playbackHandle: handle,\n209:       );\n210:       await tester.pumpWidget(MaterialApp(home: plugin.build(ctx)));\n211:       await tester.pumpAndSettle();\n212:       for (final CctvSlot slot in cctvSlots) {\n213:         expect(find.text(slot.defaultLabel), findsOneWidget);\n214:       }\n215:       expect(find.textContaining('clip-0'), findsNothing);\n216:     });\n217: \n218:     testWidgets('custom-label manifest drives wall slot labels end-to-end',\n219:         (WidgetTester tester) async {\n220:       // Owner Q3: labels are config-driven. A manifest whose clips carry\n221:       // `label` must drive the HUD text on the matching camera slot, while\n222:       // slots without a label keep the core_playlist default.\n223:       final _FakeHandle handle = _FakeHandle();\n224:       final HauntedSurveillancePlugin plugin = HauntedSurveillancePlugin(\n225:         disableEffects: true,\n226:         manifest: _manifest(\n227:           labels: const <String, String?>{\n228:             'CAM-01': 'Front Door',\n229:             'CAM-02': null,\n230:             'CAM-03': 'Basement',\n231:             'CAM-04': '   ',\n232:           },\n233:         ),\n234:         tileBuilder: _fakeSurface,\n235:       );\n236:       final ChannelContext ctx = ChannelContext(\n237:         partyId: PartyId('party-1'),\n238:         playbackHandle: handle,\n239:       );\n240:       await tester.pumpWidget(MaterialApp(home: plugin.build(ctx)));\n241:       await tester.pumpAndSettle();\n242:       expect(find.text('Front Door'), findsOneWidget);\n243:       expect(find.text('CAM-02 · kitchen'), findsOneWidget);\n244:       expect(find.text('Basement'), findsOneWidget);\n245:       expect(find.text('CAM-04 · storage room'), findsOneWidget);\n246:       // Blank labels are not rendered as-is.\n247:       expect(find.text('   '), findsNothing);\n248:     });\n249: \n250:     testWidgets('slots follow camera identity, not manifest clip order',\n251:         (WidgetTester tester) async {\n252:       final _FakeHandle handle = _FakeHandle();\n253:       final HauntedSurveillancePlugin plugin = HauntedSurveillancePlugin(\n254:         disableEffects: true,\n255:         manifest: _manifest(\n256:           labels: const <String, String?>{\n257:             'CAM-01': 'Front Door',\n258:             'CAM-02': 'Kitchen Cam',\n259:             'CAM-03': 'Stairs',\n260:             'CAM-04': 'Vault',\n261:           },\n262:           reverseClipOrder: true,\n263:         ),\n264:         tileBuilder: _fakeSurface,\n265:       );\n266:       final ChannelContext ctx = ChannelContext(\n267:         partyId: PartyId('party-1'),\n268:         playbackHandle: handle,\n269:       );\n270:       await tester.pumpWidget(MaterialApp(home: plugin.build(ctx)));\n271:       await tester.pumpAndSettle();\n272:       // Labels are placed by camera id, so reversed clip order still puts\n273:       // CAM-01's label on wall slot 0.\n274:       final Text first = tester.widget<Text>(find.text('Front Door'));\n275:       expect(first.data, 'Front Door');\n276:       expect(\n277:         tester.getTopLeft(find.text('Front Door')).dx,\n278:         lessThan(tester.getTopLeft(find.text('Kitchen Cam')).dx),\n279:       );\n280:       expect(\n281:         tester.getTopLeft(find.text('Stairs')).dy,\n282:         greaterThan(tester.getTopLeft(find.text('Kitchen Cam')).dy),\n283:       );\n284:     });\n285: \n286:     testWidgets('unknown-camera manifest degrades to defaults per slot',\n287:         (WidgetTester tester) async {\n288:       // Validation rejects unknown camera ids upstream (core_playlist), but\n289:       // a stale payload must never crash the wall: an unmatched clip is\n290:       // ignored and its slot keeps the canonical default.\n291:       final _FakeHandle handle = _FakeHandle();\n292:       final HauntedSurveillancePlugin plugin = HauntedSurveillancePlugin(\n293:         disableEffects: true,\n294:         manifest: PlaybackManifest(\n295:           partyId: 'party-1',\n296:           channelId: hauntedSurveillanceChannelId,\n297:           version: 3,\n298:           publishedAt: DateTime.utc(2026, 10, 31, 20),\n299:           clips: <ClipDescriptor>[\n300:             for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++)\n301:               ClipDescriptor(\n302:                 id: 'clip-0$i',\n303:                 cameraId: 'CAM-0${i + 1}',\n304:                 storageObjectId: 'obj-0$i',\n305:                 sha256: _sha,\n306:                 sizeBytes: 1024,\n307:                 duration: const Duration(seconds: 4),\n308:                 mimeType: 'video/mp4',\n309:               ),\n310:             const ClipDescriptor(\n311:               id: 'clip-99',\n312:               cameraId: 'CAM-09',\n313:               storageObjectId: 'obj-99',\n314:               sha256: _sha,\n315:               sizeBytes: 1024,\n316:               duration: Duration(seconds: 4),\n317:               mimeType: 'video/mp4',\n318:               label: 'Rodent Cam',\n319:             ),\n320:           ],\n321:         ),\n322:         tileBuilder: _fakeSurface,\n323:       );\n324:       final ChannelContext ctx = ChannelContext(\n325:         partyId: PartyId('party-1'),\n326:         playbackHandle: handle,\n327:       );\n328:       await tester.pumpWidget(MaterialApp(home: plugin.build(ctx)));\n329:       await tester.pumpAndSettle();\n330:       expect(tester.takeException(), isNull);\n331:       expect(find.text('Rodent Cam'), findsNothing);\n332:       for (final CctvSlot slot in cctvSlots) {\n333:         expect(find.text(slot.defaultLabel), findsOneWidget);\n334:       }\n335:     });\n336: \n337:     testWidgets('manifest overlay tunes the tile effect intensities',\n338:         (WidgetTester tester) async {\n339:       final HauntedSurveillancePlugin plugin = HauntedSurveillancePlugin(\n340:         manifest: _manifest(\n341:           overlay: const OverlaySettings(\n342:             scanlineOpacity: 0.8,\n343:             noiseLevel: 0.05,\n344:             vignette: 0.3,\n345:           ),\n346:         ),\n347:         tileBuilder: _fakeSurface,\n348:         clock: _FakeClock(DateTime(2026, 10, 31, 20)),\n349:       );\n350:       final ChannelContext ctx = ChannelContext(\n351:         partyId: PartyId('party-1'),\n352:         playbackHandle: _FakeHandle(),\n353:       );\n354:       await tester.pumpWidget(MaterialApp(home: plugin.build(ctx)));\n355:       await tester.pumpAndSettle();\n356: \n357:       final Iterable<CustomPaint> scanlines = tester.widgetList<CustomPaint>(\n358:         find.byWidgetPredicate(\n359:           (Widget w) => w is CustomPaint && w.painter is ScanlinesPainter,\n360:         ),\n361:       );\n362:       expect(scanlines, hasLength(4));\n363:       expect(\n364:         (scanlines.first.painter! as ScanlinesPainter).opacity,\n365:         closeTo(0.1 + 0.25 * 0.8, 1e-9),\n366:       );\n367: \n368:       final Iterable<CustomPaint> vignettes = tester.widgetList<CustomPaint>(\n369:         find.byWidgetPredicate(\n370:           (Widget w) => w is CustomPaint && w.painter is VignettePainter,\n371:         ),\n372:       );\n373:       expect(vignettes, hasLength(4));\n374:       expect((vignettes.first.painter! as VignettePainter).strength, 0.3);\n375:     });\n376: \n377:     testWidgets('default wall wires scanline + vignette overlays per tile',\n378:         (WidgetTester tester) async {\n379:       final HauntedSurveillancePlugin plugin = HauntedSurveillancePlugin(\n380:         tileBuilder: _fakeSurface,\n381:         clock: _FakeClock(DateTime(2026, 10, 31, 20)),\n382:       );\n383:       final ChannelContext ctx = ChannelContext(\n384:         partyId: PartyId('party-1'),\n385:         playbackHandle: _FakeHandle(),\n386:       );\n387:       await tester.pumpWidget(MaterialApp(home: plugin.build(ctx)));\n388:       await tester.pumpAndSettle();\n389: \n390:       final Finder scanlines = find.byWidgetPredicate(\n391:         (Widget w) => w is CustomPaint && w.painter is ScanlinesPainter,\n392:       );\n393:       final Finder vignette = find.byWidgetPredicate(\n394:         (Widget w) => w is CustomPaint && w.painter is VignettePainter,\n395:       );\n396:       expect(scanlines, findsNWidgets(4));\n397:       expect(vignette, findsNWidgets(4));\n398:       expect(find.byKey(const Key('surface-CAM-01')), findsOneWidget);\n399:     });\n400: \n401:     testWidgets('disableEffects removes painters from every tile',\n402:         (WidgetTester tester) async {\n403:       final HauntedSurveillancePlugin plugin = HauntedSurveillancePlugin(\n404:         disableEffects: true,\n405:         tileBuilder: _fakeSurface,\n406:         clock: _FakeClock(DateTime(2026, 10, 31, 20)),\n407:       );\n408:       final ChannelContext ctx = ChannelContext(\n409:         partyId: PartyId('party-1'),\n410:         playbackHandle: _FakeHandle(),\n411:       );\n412:       await tester.pumpWidget(MaterialApp(home: plugin.build(ctx)));\n413:       await tester.pumpAndSettle();\n414:       expect(\n415:         find.byWidgetPredicate(\n416:           (Widget w) => w is CustomPaint && w.painter is ScanlinesPainter,\n417:         ),\n418:         findsNothing,\n419:       );\n420:     });\n421: \n422:     testWidgets('coordinator boot failure degrades to SignalLost, wall survives',\n423:         (WidgetTester tester) async {\n424:       const HauntedSurveillancePlugin plugin = HauntedSurveillancePlugin(\n425:         disableEffects: true,\n426:         tileBuilder: _fakeSurface,\n427:       );\n428:       final ChannelContext ctx = ChannelContext(\n429:         partyId: PartyId('party-1'),\n430:         playbackHandle: _FailingHandle(),\n431:       );\n432:       await tester.pumpWidget(MaterialApp(home: plugin.build(ctx)));\n433:       await tester.pumpAndSettle();\n434:       expect(find.text('SIGNAL LOST'), findsNWidgets(4));\n435:       expect(tester.takeException(), isNull);\n436:     });\n437: \n438:     testWidgets('a throwing surface degrades to SignalLost, wall survives',\n439:         (WidgetTester tester) async {\n440:       const HauntedSurveillancePlugin plugin = HauntedSurveillancePlugin(\n441:         disableEffects: true,\n442:         tileBuilder: _throwingSurface,\n443:       );\n444:       final ChannelContext ctx = ChannelContext(\n445:         partyId: PartyId('party-1'),\n446:         playbackHandle: _FakeHandle(),\n447:       );\n448:       await tester.pumpWidget(MaterialApp(home: plugin.build(ctx)));\n449:       await tester.pumpAndSettle();\n450:       expect(find.text('SIGNAL LOST'), findsNWidgets(4));\n451:       expect(tester.takeException(), isNull);\n452:     });\n453: \n454:     testWidgets('build applies wall config from ChannelContext.settings',\n455:         (WidgetTester tester) async {\n456:       // Constructor leaves effects on, but the host disables them via the\n457:       // channel contract: settings win without re-instantiating the plugin.\n458:       final HauntedSurveillancePlugin plugin = HauntedSurveillancePlugin(\n459:         tileBuilder: _fakeSurface,\n460:         clock: _FakeClock(DateTime(2026, 10, 31, 20)),\n461:       );\n462:       final ChannelContext ctx = ChannelContext(\n463:         partyId: PartyId('party-1'),\n464:         playbackHandle: _FakeHandle(),\n465:         settings: const ChannelSettings(<String, Object?>{\n466:           'effectsDisabled': true,\n467:           'manifestVersion': 7,\n468:           'overscanSafe': true,\n469:           'labels': <String, String>{'CAM-01': 'PORCH · custom'},\n470:         }),\n471:       );\n472:       await tester.pumpWidget(MaterialApp(home: plugin.build(ctx)));\n473:       await tester.pumpAndSettle();\n474: \n475:       expect(\n476:         find.byWidgetPredicate(\n477:           (Widget w) => w is CustomPaint && w.painter is ScanlinesPainter,\n478:         ),\n479:         findsNothing,\n480:         reason: 'settings effectsDisabled must drop overlays',\n481:       );\n482:       expect(find.text('PORCH · custom'), findsOneWidget);\n483:       expect(find.text('CAM-02 · kitchen'), findsOneWidget);\n484:       expect(tester.takeException(), isNull);\n485:     });\n486: \n487:     testWidgets('constructor wall config still applies with empty settings',\n488:         (WidgetTester tester) async {\n489:       final HauntedSurveillancePlugin plugin = HauntedSurveillancePlugin(\n490:         disableEffects: true,\n491:         tileBuilder: _fakeSurface,\n492:         clock: _FakeClock(DateTime(2026, 10, 31, 20)),\n493:       );\n494:       final ChannelContext ctx = ChannelContext(\n495:         partyId: PartyId('party-1'),\n496:         playbackHandle: _FakeHandle(),\n497:       );\n498:       await tester.pumpWidget(MaterialApp(home: plugin.build(ctx)));\n499:       await tester.pumpAndSettle();\n500: \n501:       expect(\n502:         find.byWidgetPredicate(\n503:           (Widget w) => w is CustomPaint && w.painter is ScanlinesPainter,\n504:         ),\n505:         findsNothing,\n506:       );\n507:       expect(find.text('CAM-01 · hallway'), findsOneWidget);\n508:       expect(tester.takeException(), isNull);\n509:     });\n510: \n511:     testWidgets('settings label overrides win over manifest clip labels',\n512:         (WidgetTester tester) async {\n513:       // Precedence composition on one wall: the manifest carries a clip\n514:       // label for CAM-01 AND settings carry an override for the same\n515:       // camera — settings win. CAM-03 keeps its manifest label, CAM-02\n516:       // and CAM-04 keep slot defaults.\n517:       final HauntedSurveillancePlugin plugin = HauntedSurveillancePlugin(\n518:         disableEffects: true,\n519:         manifest: _manifest(\n520:           labels: const <String, String?>{\n521:             'CAM-01': 'Manifest Door',\n522:             'CAM-03': 'Manifest Basement',\n523:           },\n524:         ),\n525:         tileBuilder: _fakeSurface,\n526:       );\n527:       final ChannelContext ctx = ChannelContext(\n528:         partyId: PartyId('party-1'),\n529:         playbackHandle: _FakeHandle(),\n530:         settings: const ChannelSettings(<String, Object?>{\n531:           'labels': <String, String>{'CAM-01': 'PORCH · settings'},\n532:         }),\n533:       );\n534:       await tester.pumpWidget(MaterialApp(home: plugin.build(ctx)));\n535:       await tester.pumpAndSettle();\n536: \n537:       expect(find.text('PORCH · settings'), findsOneWidget);\n538:       expect(find.text('Manifest Door'), findsNothing);\n539:       expect(find.text('Manifest Basement'), findsOneWidget);\n540:       expect(find.text('CAM-02 · kitchen'), findsOneWidget);\n541:       expect(find.text('CAM-04 · storage room'), findsOneWidget);\n542:       expect(tester.takeException(), isNull);\n543:     });\n544: \n545:     test('cctvLabelOverridesFromSettings filters non-Map/non-string shapes',\n546:         () {\n547:       // No `labels` key at all.\n548:       expect(\n549:         cctvLabelOverridesFromSettings(const ChannelSettings()),\n550:         isEmpty,\n551:       );\n552:       // Non-Map value is ignored, not thrown on.\n553:       expect(\n554:         cctvLabelOverridesFromSettings(\n555:           const ChannelSettings(<String, Object?>{'labels': 'PORCH'}),\n556:         ),\n557:         isEmpty,\n558:       );\n559:       // Non-string keys/values are dropped; only String->String survives.\n560:       expect(\n561:         cctvLabelOverridesFromSettings(\n562:           const ChannelSettings(<String, Object?>{\n563:             'labels': <Object?, Object?>{\n564:               'CAM-01': 'Porch',\n565:               'CAM-02': 42,\n566:               'CAM-03': null,\n567:               7: 'Attic',\n568:             },\n569:           }),\n570:         ),\n571:         <String, String>{'CAM-01': 'Porch'},\n572:       );\n573:     });\n574:   });\n575: \n576:   group('port direction (D-08)', () {\n577:     // Finding D-08: channels must be able to consume the control-plane ports\n578:     // without importing `infra_*`. These two tests keep that true from the\n579:     // consumer side: one walks the real import graph, the other compiles and\n580:     // runs fakes implemented purely against `channel_api`.\n581:     test('lib graph of this channel imports no infra_* package', () {\n582:       final Set<String> visitedPackages = <String>{};\n583:       final List<File> sources = _transitiveLibSources(\n584:         Directory.current,\n585:         visitedPackages,\n586:       );\n587:       expect(\n588:         visitedPackages,\n589:         containsAll(<String>['channel_cctv', 'channel_api']),\n590:         reason: 'walk must actually reach the contracts package',\n591:       );\n592:       final List<String> offenders = <String>[\n593:         for (final File f in sources)\n594:           if (f.readAsStringSync().contains('package:infra_')) f.path,\n595:       ];\n596:       expect(\n597:         offenders,\n598:         isEmpty,\n599:         reason: 'channels must not import infra_* (finding D-08)',\n600:       );\n601:     });\n602: \n603:     test('ports are implementable from channel_api alone', () async {\n604:       final _ContractOnlyManifestSource source = _ContractOnlyManifestSource(\n605:         _manifest(),\n606:       );\n607:       final ManifestSource<PlaybackManifest> port = source;\n608:       final List<PlaybackManifest> seen = await port\n609:           .watchCurrent(partyId: 'party-1', channelId: hauntedSurveillanceChannelId)\n610:           .toList();\n611:       expect(seen, hasLength(1));\n612:       expect(seen.single.channelId, hauntedSurveillanceChannelId);\n613: \n614:       final SettingsPort settings = _ContractOnlySettings();\n615:       await settings.setString(\n616:         partyId: PartyId('party-1'),\n617:         key: 'label.cam-01',\n618:         value: 'Front Door',\n619:       );\n620:       expect(\n621:         await settings.getString(\n622:           partyId: PartyId('party-1'),\n623:           key: 'label.cam-01',\n624:         ),\n625:         'Front Door',\n626:       );\n627:     });\n628:   });\n629: }\n630: \n631: \n632: /// Collects the `lib/` sources of [packageRoot] and, transitively, of every\n633: /// sibling path package reachable through `package:<name>/<path>` imports.\n634: ///\n635: /// Only local siblings (`<packages>/<name>/lib/*.dart`) are followed, so SDK\n636: /// and pub-cache packages terminate the walk. Names are recorded in\n637: /// [visited] so the caller can assert the graph was not vacuous.\n638: List<File> _transitiveLibSources(Directory packageRoot, Set<String> visited) {\n639:   final List<File> collected = <File>[];\n640:   final List<(String, Directory)> queue = <(String, Directory)>[\n641:     (_packageNameOf(packageRoot), packageRoot),\n642:   ];\n643:   while (queue.isNotEmpty) {\n644:     final (String name, Directory root) = queue.removeLast();\n645:     if (!visited.add(name)) {\n646:       continue;\n647:     }\n648:     final Directory lib = Directory('${root.path}/lib');\n649:     if (!lib.existsSync()) {\n650:       continue;\n651:     }\n652:     for (final File file in lib.listSync(recursive: true).whereType<File>()) {\n653:       if (!file.path.endsWith('.dart')) {\n654:         continue;\n655:       }\n656:       collected.add(file);\n657:       for (final String uri in _packageUrisOf(file.readAsStringSync())) {\n658:         final String target = uri.split('/').first;\n659:         final Directory sibling = Directory('${packageRoot.parent.path}/$target');\n660:         if (sibling.existsSync()) {\n661:           queue.add((target, sibling));\n662:         }\n663:       }\n664:     }\n665:   }\n666:   return collected;\n667: }\n668: \n669: /// Package name of [root], read from its `pubspec.yaml` name line.\n670: String _packageNameOf(Directory root) {\n671:   final File pubspec = File('${root.path}/pubspec.yaml');\n672:   for (final String line in pubspec.readAsLinesSync()) {\n673:     if (line.startsWith('name:')) {\n674:       return line.substring('name:'.length).trim();\n675:     }\n676:   }\n677:   return root.uri.pathSegments.where((String s) => s.isNotEmpty).last;\n678: }\n679: \n680: /// `package:<name>/<path>` URIs referenced by [source].\n681: Iterable<String> _packageUrisOf(String source) sync* {\n682:   for (final RegExpMatch match\n683:       in RegExp(r'package:([a-z0-9_]+/[A-Za-z0-9_./]+)')\n684:           .allMatches(source)) {\n685:     yield match.group(1)!;\n686:   }\n687: }\n688: \n689: /// Manifest source bound to `PlaybackManifest` using only the contracts port.\n690: final class _ContractOnlyManifestSource\n691:     implements ManifestSource<PlaybackManifest> {\n692:   _ContractOnlyManifestSource(this.manifest);\n693: \n694:   final PlaybackManifest manifest;\n695: \n696:   @override\n697:   Stream<PlaybackManifest> watchCurrent({\n698:     required String partyId,\n699:     required String channelId,\n700:   }) async* {\n701:     yield manifest;\n702:   }\n703: }\n704: \n705: /// Settings store written against the contracts port; no infra adapter used.\n706: final class _ContractOnlySettings implements SettingsPort {\n707:   final Map<String, String> _values = <String, String>{};\n708: \n709:   @override\n710:   Future<String?> getString({\n711:     required PartyId partyId,\n712:     required String key,\n713:   }) async => _values['${partyId.value}/$key'];\n714: \n715:   @override\n716:   Future<void> setString({\n717:     required PartyId partyId,\n718:     required String key,\n719:     required String value,\n720:   }) async {\n721:     _values['${partyId.value}/$key'] = value;\n722:   }\n723: \n724:   @override\n725:   Future<bool?> getBool({\n726:     required PartyId partyId,\n727:     required String key,\n728:   }) async => _values['${partyId.value}/$key'] == 'true';\n729: \n730:   @override\n731:   Future<void> setBool({\n732:     required PartyId partyId,\n733:     required String key,\n734:     required bool value,\n735:   }) async {\n736:     _values['${partyId.value}/$key'] = '$value';\n737:   }\n738: }\n739: \n740: Widget _fakeSurface(\n741:   BuildContext context,\n742:   int index,\n743:   String label,\n744:   String cameraId,\n745: ) =>\n746:     Container(color: Colors.black, key: Key('surface-$cameraId'));\n747: \n748: Widget _throwingSurface(\n749:   BuildContext context,\n750:   int index,\n751:   String label,\n752:   String cameraId,\n753: ) {\n754:   throw StateError('no decoder in tests');\n755: }\n756: \n757: /// Inline stand-in for a sibling channel's descriptor id contract.\n758: final class _SiblingStubPlugin implements ChannelPlugin {\n759:   const _SiblingStubPlugin();\n760: \n761:   @override\n762:   ChannelDescriptor get descriptor => const ChannelDescriptor(\n763:         id: 'retro_horror',\n764:         title: 'Retro Horror',\n765:         version: 1,\n766:       );\n767: \n768:   @override\n769:   Widget build(ChannelContext context) => const SizedBox.shrink();\n770: }"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false,"state":{"itemId":"fc_01a192a5ad21772f8dcfd597e1ee9687"}},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-2/packages/channel_cctv/test/channel_cctv_test.dart\"}"},"time"