,\"schemaVersion\":1,\"version\":1},\"4\":{\"cameraClips\":[{\"cameraId\":\"CAM-01\",\"durationMs\":2000,\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"objectPath\":\"parties/pilot/channels/main/delivery/1/CAM-01.mp4\",\"sha256\":\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\",\"sizeBytes\":12345},{\"cameraId\":\"CAM-02\",\"durationMs\":2000,\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"objectPath\":\"parties/pilot/channels/main/delivery/1/CAM-02.mp4\",\"sha256\":\"bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\",\"sizeBytes\":12346},{\"cameraId\":\"CAM-03\",\"durationMs\":2000,\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"objectPath\":\"parties/pilot/channels/main/delivery/1/CAM-03.mp4\",\"sha256\":\"cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc\",\"sizeBytes\":12347},{\"cameraId\":\"CAM-04\",\"durationMs\":2000,\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"objectPath\":\"parties/pilot/channels/main/delivery/1/CAM-04.mp4\",\"sha256\":\"dddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddd\",\"sizeBytes\":12348}],\"channelId\":\"main\",\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"jobId\":\"job-1\",\"partyId\":\"pilot\",\"schemaVersion\":1,\"version\":1}},\"notes\":\"Supported TV layouts are 1, 2, or 4 cameras; the camera set must equal the first-N canonical slots. Four is the default when cameraCount is absent/invalid/unreadable. Generation presets keep producing 4 clips; cameraCount is a display cap only.\"}---FIX2---\n{\"callables\":[\"createHostInvite\",\"joinHost\",\"listHostVideos\",\"generateHostVideo\",\"getHostVideoPreview\",\"deleteHostVideo\"],\"createHostInvite\":{\"request\":{\"channelId\":\"main\",\"deviceId\":\"tv-pilot\",\"partyId\":\"pilot\"},\"response\":{\"channelId\":\"main\",\"expiresAt\":\"<iso8601>\",\"inviteToken\":\"<server-minted hi-... capability>\",\"partyId\":\"pilot\"}},\"guestJoin\":{\"request\":{\"channelId\":\"main\",\"deviceId\":\"p-guest-1\",\"joinPin\":\"004201\",\"partyId\":\"pilot\"},\"response\":{\"channelId\":\"main\",\"created\":true,\"deviceId\":\"p-guest-1\",\"partyId\":\"pilot\",\"role\":\"guest\",\"status\":\"active\"}},\"hostJoin\":{\"request\":{\"channelId\":\"main\",\"deviceId\":\"p-host-1\",\"inviteToken\":\"<server-minted hi-... capability>\",\"partyId\":\"pilot\"},\"response\":{\"channelId\":\"main\",\"created\":true,\"deviceId\":\"p-host-1\",\"partyId\":\"pilot\",\"role\":\"host\",\"status\":\"active\"}},\"notes\":\"Only a registered TV may mint a host invite (short-lived, token hash stored, party/channel/expiry bound). Redemption is transactional for a separate phone identity with the server-assigned host role; same-device retries are idempotent, other-device replay, expiry, guest PIN reuse, and client-only role changes never grant host. Legacy joinParty remains guest-only.\"}---DOC---\ncommit 7a618a688af096bbed79e0209e83221b4001b9b9\nAuthor: Joaquin Beltran <contact@joaquinmx.com>\nDate:   Sat Oct 31 09:47:51 2026 -0600\n\n    cycle-12 p1: 1/2/4 camera contracts + host admin backend\n\ndiff --git a/docs/backend-contract-v1.md b/docs/backend-contract-v1.md\nindex 024c0f4..1383255 100644\n--- a/docs/backend-contract-v1.md\n+++ b/docs/backend-contract-v1.md\n@@ -34,6 +34,12 @@ an idempotency key.\n | `completeGuestUpload` | callable | party/device-scoped guest |\n | `getGuestMediaStatus` | callable | party/device-scoped guest |\n | `withdrawGuestMedia` | callable | party/device-scoped guest |\n+| `createHostInvite` | callable | registered TV only |\n+| `joinHost` | callable | phone with a valid host invite |\n+| `listHostVideos` | callable | registered host only |\n+| `generateHostVideo` | callable | registered host only |\n+| `getHostVideoPreview` | callable | registered host only |\n+| `deleteHostVideo` | callable | registered host only |\n \n Guest ingest objects live under\n `parties/{partyId}/guests/{deviceId}/ingest/{submissionId}/photo.jpg` with\n@@ -45,19 +51,106 @@ Firestore guest consent/media docs are callable-only (explicit deny in\n \n Firestore layout: `parties/{partyId}` (`ownerUid`, `status`, `activeChannelId`),\n `channels/{channelId}`, `manifests/current_{channelId}` (`version`,\n-`cameraClips[4]`, `schemaVersion`, stable publication `createdAt`),\n+`cameraClips[1|2|4]`, `schemaVersion`, stable publication `createdAt`),\n `jobs/{jobId}` (state machine\n `queued → running → ready → delivering → purged`, plus `failed`/`expired` with\n sanitized `errorCode`, `modelId`, `costEstimate`), `devices/{deviceId}`,\n-`deliveryAcks/{ackId}`.\n+`deliveryAcks/{ackId}`, `hostInvites/{inviteId}` (token hash, party/channel/\n+expiry binding), `seedVideos/{seedId}` (status, job link, preview refs).\n \n Storage layout: `parties/{partyId}/channels/{channelId}/delivery/{version}/{camera}.mp4`\n (served only via short-lived signed URLs minted after callable checks; rules\n-deny all direct client reads/writes). `ingest/` and `generated/{jobId}/`\n+deny all direct client reads/writes). `hostPreviews/{seedId}/{camera}.mp4`\n+are separately referenced preview objects with their own TTL metadata (same\n+deny-all rules; signed on demand, never persisted). `ingest/` and\n+`generated/{jobId}/`\n prefixes are worker-internal. Lifecycle TTL (`storage.lifecycle.json`,\n `daysSinceCustomTime: 1` on `parties/`) is defense-in-depth behind\n `sweepExpiredMedia`.\n \n+## Camera counts (configurable 1/2/4 layouts)\n+\n+Supported manifest clip counts are exactly 1, 2, or 4; four remains the\n+default when the `cameraCount` setting is absent, invalid, or unreadable.\n+`cameraCount` (a SettingsPort display cap, owned by other partitions) never\n+changes what the backend publishes: generation presets keep producing 4\n+clips, and reduced layouts still prepare + ACK the complete received\n+manifest. Validators on both sides (`validateCctvManifest` in\n+`core_playlist`, `validateCanonicalClips`/`parseAck` in `contracts.ts`,\n+Dart delivery URL/ACK checks in `firebase_delivery_client.dart`) require the\n+camera set to equal the first-N canonical slots in wall order\n+(`CAM-01` for 1; `CAM-01`–`CAM-02` for 2; all four for 4). Reordered valid\n+clips remain accepted; unsupported counts, gaps (e.g. `{CAM-01, CAM-03}`\n+for count 2), duplicates, unknown cameras, and invalid existing metadata\n+are rejected. ACK validation is exact at acceptance: the hash set must equal\n+the actual manifest's camera set with identical digests, so extra hashes are\n+rejected both at shape time (`parseAck`) and against the stored manifest\n+(`canonicalClipsMatch`) and on accepted-ACK replay. Legacy four-camera\n+fixture hashes and the ACK idempotency key are unchanged\n+(`test/fixtures/backend_contract_v1.json`); count vectors live in\n+`test/fixtures/cctv_counts_v1.json`.\n+\n+## Host entry and administration\n+\n+The companion uses a dedicated host entry screen (`HostEntryScreen` with\n+Scan Host QR + an explicit Join-as-guest route; companion/TV UI owned by\n+other partitions). Rationale: guest PIN admission is intentionally broad —\n+anyone who can see the TV screen can self-register as a guest with full\n+party-scoped read/generate/ACK power — so host administration must never be\n+reachable through the guest PIN or a client-supplied role string. A separate\n+server-minted, short-lived invite capability keeps the two routes visibly\n+distinct and makes the privilege boundary auditable: the QR payload, the\n+Firestore role, and the callable gates all distinguish host from guest.\n+\n+- `createHostInvite { partyId, deviceId, channelId }` (TV-only caller:\n+  registered device with `role: \"tv\"`, else `FORBIDDEN`) mints a short-lived\n+  (`HOST_INVITE_TTL_MS`, 5 minutes) invite. The token (`hi-…`) is returned\n+  once; only its SHA-256 hash is stored at\n+  `parties/{partyId}/hostInvites/{inviteId}`, bound to party/channel/expiry.\n+- `joinHost { partyId, deviceId, channelId, inviteToken }` redeems the invite\n+  transactionally for a separate phone identity with the server-assigned\n+  host role. Same-device redemption retries are idempotent (`created:\n+  false`); other-device replay, expiry, cross-party/cross-channel reuse,\n+  guest PIN reuse (six-digit strings are shape-rejected as tokens), and\n+  client-supplied role fields (ignored; the role is always written\n+  server-side) can never grant host access.\n+- Legacy `joinParty` remains guest-only: it writes `role: \"guest\"`\n+  server-side, rejects re-registration of non-guest (host/tv) device docs,\n+  and never upgrades a role.\n+- Every administrative operation (`listHostVideos`, `generateHostVideo`,\n+  `getHostVideoPreview`, `deleteHostVideo`) revalidates the registered host\n+  role and party/channel scope (`assertRegisteredHostDevice`); guests get\n+  `FORBIDDEN`. Role examples live in `test/fixtures/join_roles_v1.json`.\n+\n+## Host seed catalog\n+\n+`listHostVideos` serves a server-backed seed catalog at\n+`parties/{partyId}/seedVideos/{seedId}` containing generation status and\n+camera video references. `generateHostVideo { partyId, deviceId, channelId,\n+seedId, idempotencyKey, presetId?, guestMediaId? }` is a scoped entry point\n+to the existing fixed-preset queue with the same idempotency, single-flight\n+budget, and consent checks as `requestGeneration` (the backing job is\n+`hv-{seedId}`); queue deduplication and rebinding refusal behave identically.\n+`getHostVideoPreview { …, seedId }` materializes separately referenced,\n+TTL-limited (`HOST_PREVIEW_TTL_MS`, 24h) preview objects under\n+`hostPreviews/{seedId}/…` before delivery objects can be ACK-purged and\n+signs them on demand without persisting signed URLs.\n+\n+Deletion granularity and expiry: `deleteHostVideo { …, seedIds[] }`\n+(deleted per selected seed id) removes the seed entries and their associated\n+preview + delivery objects, revokes an affected current manifest whose jobId\n+matches a deleted seed, and preserves accounting records (costLogs/usage\n+ledger rows are never deleted). A job tombstone (`hostDeleted`) is written\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"cameraIds\":[\"CAM-01\",\"CAM-02\",\"CAM-03\",\"CAM-04\"],\"counts\":[1,2,4],\"defaultCount\":4,\"invalid\":{\"duplicateCamera\":{\"cameraClips\":[{\"cameraId\":\"CAM-01\",\"durationMs\":2000,\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"objectPath\":\"parties/pilot/channels/main/delivery/1/CAM-01.mp4\",\"sha256\":\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\",\"sizeBytes\":12345},{\"cameraId\":\"CAM-01\",\"durationMs\":2000,\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"objectPath\":\"parties/pilot/channels/main/delivery/1/CAM-01.mp4\",\"sha256\":\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\",\"sizeBytes\":12345}]},\"gapCount2\":{\"cameraClips\":[{\"cameraId\":\"CAM-01\",\"durationMs\":2000,\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"objectPath\":\"parties/pilot/channels/main/delivery/1/CAM-01.mp4\",\"sha256\":\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\",\"sizeBytes\":12345},{\"cameraId\":\"CAM-03\",\"durationMs\":2000,\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"objectPath\":\"parties/pilot/channels/main/delivery/1/CAM-03.mp4\",\"sha256\":\"cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc\",\"sizeBytes\":12347}]},\"threeClips\":{\"cameraClips\":[{\"cameraId\":\"CAM-01\",\"durationMs\":2000,\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"objectPath\":\"parties/pilot/channels/main/delivery/1/CAM-01.mp4\",\"sha256\":\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\",\"sizeBytes\":12345},{\"cameraId\":\"CAM-02\",\"durationMs\":2000,\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"objectPath\":\"parties/pilot/channels/main/delivery/1/CAM-02.mp4\",\"sha256\":\"bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\",\"sizeBytes\":12346},{\"cameraId\":\"CAM-03\",\"durationMs\":2000,\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"objectPath\":\"parties/pilot/channels/main/delivery/1/CAM-03.mp4\",\"sha256\":\"cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc\",\"sizeBytes\":12347}]},\"unknownCamera\":{\"cameraClips\":[{\"cameraId\":\"CAM-05\",\"durationMs\":2000,\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"objectPath\":\"parties/pilot/channels/main/delivery/1/CAM-05.mp4\",\"sha256\":\"eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee\",\"sizeBytes\":12349}]}},\"manifests\":{\"1\":{\"cameraClips\":[{\"cameraId\":\"CAM-01\",\"durationMs\":2000,\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"objectPath\":\"parties/pilot/channels/main/delivery/1/CAM-01.mp4\",\"sha256\":\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\",\"sizeBytes\":12345}],\"channelId\":\"main\",\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"jobId\":\"job-1\",\"partyId\":\"pilot\",\"schemaVersion\":1,\"version\":1},\"2\":{\"cameraClips\":[{\"cameraId\":\"CAM-01\",\"durationMs\":2000,\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"objectPath\":\"parties/pilot/channels/main/delivery/1/CAM-01.mp4\",\"sha256\":\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\",\"sizeBytes\":12345},{\"cameraId\":\"CAM-02\",\"durationMs\":2000,\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"objectPath\":\"parties/pilot/channels/main/delivery/1/CAM-02.mp4\",\"sha256\":\"bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\",\"sizeBytes\":12346}],\"channelId\":\"main\",\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"jobId\":\"job-1\",\"partyId\":\"pilot\",\"schemaVersion\":1,\"version\":1},\"4\":{\"cameraClips\":[{\"cameraId\":\"CAM-01\",\"durationMs\":2000,\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"objectPath\":\"parties/pilot/channels/main/delivery/1/CAM-01.mp4\",\"sha256\":\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\",\"sizeBytes\":12345},{\"cameraId\":\"CAM-02\",\"durationMs\":2000,\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"objectPath\":\"parties/pilot/channels/main/delivery/1/CAM-02.mp4\",\"sha256\":\"bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\",\"sizeBytes\":12346},{\"cameraId\":\"CAM-03\",\"durationMs\":2000,\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"objectPath\":\"parties/pilot/channels/main/delivery/1/CAM-03.mp4\",\"sha256\":\"cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc\",\"sizeBytes\":12347},{\"cameraId\":\"CAM-04\",\"durationMs\":2000,\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"objectPath\":\"parties/pilot/channels/main/delivery/1/CAM-04.mp4\",\"sha256\":\"dddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddd\",\"sizeBytes\":12348}],\"channelId\":\"main\",\"expiresAt\":\"2026-11-29T15:00:00.000Z\",\"jobId\":\"job-1\",\"partyId\":\"pilot\",\"schemaVersion\":1,\"version\":1}},\"notes\":\"Supported TV layouts are 1, 2, or 4 cameras; the camera set must equal the first-N canonical slots. Four is the default when cameraCount is absent/invalid/unreadable. Generation presets keep producing 4 clips; cameraCount is a display cap only.\"}---FIX2---\n{\"callables\":[\"createHostInvite\",\"joinHost\",\"listHostVideos\",\"generateHostVideo\",\"getHostVideoPreview\",\"deleteHostVideo\"],\"createHostInvite\":{\"request\":{\"channelId\":\"main\",\"deviceId\":\"tv-pilot\",\"partyId\":\"pilot\"},\"response\":{\"channelId\":\"main\",\"expiresAt\":\"<iso8601>\",\"inviteToken\":\"<server-minted hi-... capability>\",\"partyId\":\"pilot\"}},\"guestJoin\":{\"request\":{\"channelId\":\"main\",\"deviceId\":\"p-guest-1\",\"joinPin\":\"004201\",\"partyId\":\"pilot\"},\"response\":{\"channelId\":\"main\",\"created\":true,\"deviceId\":\"p-guest-1\",\"partyId\":\"pilot\",\"role\":\"guest\",\"status\":\"active\"}},\"hostJoin\":{\"request\":{\"channelId\":\"main\",\"deviceId\":\"p-host-1\",\"inviteToken\":\"<server-minted hi-... capability>\",\"partyId\":\"pilot\"},\"response\":{\"channelId\":\"main\",\"created\":true,\"deviceId\":\"p-host-1\",\"partyId\":\"pilot\",\"role\":\"host\",\"status\":\"active\"}},\"notes\":\"Only a registered TV may mint a host invite (short-lived, token hash stored, party/channel/expiry bound). Redemption is transactional for a separate phone identity with the server-assigned host role; same-device retries are idempotent, other-device replay, expiry, guest PIN reuse, and client-only role changes never grant host. Legacy joinParty remains guest-only.\"}---DOC---\ncommit 7a618a688af096bbed79e0209e83221b4001b9b9\nAuthor: Joaquin Beltran <contact@joaquinmx.com>\nDate:   Sat Oct 31 09:47:51 2026 -0600\n\n    cycle-12 p1: 1/2/4 camera contracts + host admin backend\n\ndiff --git a/docs/backend-contract-v1.md b/docs/backend-contract-v1.md\nindex 024c0f4..1383255 100644\n--- a/docs/backend-contract-v1.md\n+++ b/docs/backend-contract-v1.md\n@@ -34,6 +34,12 @@ an idempotency key.\n | `completeGuestUpload` | callable | party/device-scoped guest |\n | `getGuestMediaStatus` | callable | party/device-scoped guest |\n | `withdrawGuestMedia` | callable | party/device-scoped guest |\n+| `createHostInvite` | callable | registered TV only |\n+| `joinHost` | callable | phone with a valid host invite |\n+| `listHostVideos` | callable | registered host only |\n+| `generateHostVideo` | callable | registered host only |\n+| `getHostVideoPreview` | callable | registered host only |\n+| `deleteHostVideo` | callable | registered host only |\n \n Guest ingest objects live under\n `parties/{partyId}/guests/{deviceId}/ingest/{submissionId}/photo.jpg` with\n@@ -45,19 +51,106 @@ Firestore guest consent/media docs are callable-only (explicit deny in\n \n Firestore layout: `parties/{partyId}` (`ownerUid`, `status`, `activeChannelId`),\n `channels/{channelId}`, `manifests/current_{channelId}` (`version`,\n-`cameraClips[4]`, `schemaVersion`, stable publication `createdAt`),\n+`cameraClips[1|2|4]`, `schemaVersion`, stable publication `createdAt`),\n `jobs/{jobId}` (state machine\n `queued → running → ready → delivering → purged`, plus `failed`/`expired` with\n sanitized `errorCode`, `modelId`, `costEstimate`), `devices/{deviceId}`,\n-`deliveryAcks/{ackId}`.\n+`deliveryAcks/{ackId}`, `hostInvites/{inviteId}` (token hash, party/channel/\n+expiry binding), `seedVideos/{seedId}` (status, job link, preview refs).\n \n Storage layout: `parties/{partyId}/channels/{channelId}/delivery/{version}/{camera}.mp4`\n (served only via short-lived signed URLs minted after callable checks; rules\n-deny all direct client reads/writes). `ingest/` and `generated/{jobId}/`\n+deny all direct client reads/writes). `hostPreviews/{seedId}/{camera}.mp4`\n+are separately referenced preview objects with their own TTL metadata (same\n+deny-all rules; signed on demand, never persisted). `ingest/` and\n+`generated/{jobId}/`\n prefixes are worker-internal. Lifecycle TTL (`storage.lifecycle.json`,\n `daysSinceCustomTime: 1` on `parties/`) is defense-in-depth behind\n `sweepExpiredMedia`.\n \n+## Camera counts (configurable 1/2/4 layouts)\n+\n+Supported manifest clip counts are exactly 1, 2, or 4; four remains the\n+default when the `cameraCount` setting is absent, invalid, or unreadable.\n+`cameraCount` (a SettingsPort display cap, owned by other partitions) never\n+changes what the backend publishes: generation presets keep producing 4\n+clips, and reduced layouts still prepare + ACK the complete received\n+manifest. Validators on both sides (`validateCctvManifest` in\n+`core_playlist`, `validateCanonicalClips`/`parseAck` in `contracts.ts`,\n+Dart delivery URL/ACK checks in `firebase_delivery_client.dart`) require the\n+camera set to equal the first-N canonical slots in wall order\n+(`CAM-01` for 1; `CAM-01`–`CAM-02` for 2; all four for 4). Reordered valid\n+clips remain accepted; unsupported counts, gaps (e.g. `{CAM-01, CAM-03}`\n+for count 2), duplicates, unknown cameras, and invalid existing metadata\n+are rejected. ACK validation is exact at acceptance: the hash set must equal\n+the actual manifest's camera set with identical digests, so extra hashes are\n+rejected both at shape time (`parseAck`) and against the stored manifest\n+(`canonicalClipsMatch`) and on accepted-ACK replay. Legacy four-camera\n+fixture hashes and the ACK idempotency key are unchanged\n+(`test/fixtures/backend_contract_v1.json`); count vectors live in\n+`test/fixtures/cctv_counts_v1.json`.\n+\n+## Host entry and administration\n+\n+The companion uses a dedicated host entry screen (`HostEntryScreen` with\n+Scan Host QR + an explicit Join-as-guest route; companion/TV UI owned by\n+other partitions). Rationale: guest PIN admission is intentionally broad —\n+anyone who can see the TV screen can self-register as a guest with full\n+party-scoped read/generate/ACK power — so host administration must never be\n+reachable through the guest PIN or a client-supplied role string. A separate\n+server-minted, short-lived invite capability keeps the two routes visibly\n+distinct and makes the privilege boundary auditable: the QR payload, the\n+Firestore role, and the callable gates all distinguish host from guest.\n+\n+- `createHostInvite { partyId, deviceId, channelId }` (TV-only caller:\n+  registered device with `role: \"tv\"`, else `FORBIDDEN`) mints a short-lived\n+  (`HOST_INVITE_TTL_MS`, 5 minutes) invite. The token (`hi-…`) is returned\n+  once; only its SHA-256 hash is stored at\n+  `parties/{partyId}/hostInvites/{inviteId}`, bound to party/channel/expiry.\n+- `joinHost { partyId, deviceId, channelId, inviteToken }` redeems the invite\n+  transactionally for a separate phone identity with the server-assigned\n+  host role. Same-device redemption retries are idempotent (`created:\n+  false`); other-device replay, expiry, cross-party/cross-channel reuse,\n+  guest PIN reuse (six-digit strings are shape-rejected as tokens), and\n+  client-supplied role fields (ignored; the role is always written\n+  server-side) can never grant host access.\n+- Legacy `joinParty` remains guest-only: it writes `role: \"guest\"`\n+  server-side, rejects re-registration of non-guest (host/tv) device docs,\n+  and never upgrades a role.\n+- Every administrative operation (`listHostVideos`, `generateHostVideo`,\n+  `getHostVideoPreview`, `deleteHostVideo`) revalidates the registered host\n+  role and party/channel scope (`assertRegisteredHostDevice`); guests get\n+  `FORBIDDEN`. Role examples live in `test/fixtures/join_roles_v1.json`.\n+\n+## Host seed catalog\n+\n+`listHostVideos` serves a server-backed seed catalog at\n+`parties/{partyId}/seedVideos/{seedId}` containing generation status and\n+camera video references. `generateHostVideo { partyId, deviceId, channelId,\n+seedId, idempotencyKey, presetId?, guestMediaId? }` is a scoped entry point\n+to the existing fixed-preset queue with the same idempotency, single-flight\n+budget, and consent checks as `requestGeneration` (the backing job is\n+`hv-{seedId}`); queue deduplication and rebinding refusal behave identically.\n+`getHostVideoPreview { …, seedId }` materializes separately referenced,\n+TTL-limited (`HOST_PREVIEW_TTL_MS`, 24h) preview objects under\n+`hostPreviews/{seedId}/…` before delivery objects can be ACK-purged and\n+signs them on demand without persisting signed URLs.\n+\n+Deletion granularity and expiry: `deleteHostVideo { …, seedIds[] }`\n+(deleted per selected seed id) removes the seed entries and their associated\n+preview + delivery objects, revokes an affected current manifest whose jobId\n+matches a deleted seed, and preserves accounting records (costLogs/usage\n+ledger rows are never deleted). A job tombstone (`hostDeleted`) is written\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false,"state":{"itemId":"fc_01a192a5e3cd7009a820c53475fb9214"}},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cat test/fixtures/cctv_counts_v1.json; echo ---FIX2---; cat test/fixtures/join_roles_v1.json; echo ---DOC---; git show HEAD -- docs/backend-contract-v1.md | head -120\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-2\"}"},"time":{"start":1793461708453,"end