{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793462025147,"sessionID":"ses_e6d5a7eaaffeH1wroUP5Ck5Yd2","part":{"partID":"prt_192aab9a0001OkGY0wbc31o9NL","sessionID":"ses_e6d5a7eaaffeH1wroUP5Ck5Yd2","messageID":"msg_192a62613001K0566H7d8ZL8Po","type":"tool","id":"call_01a192aab94c71ff90522306de3f5a1e","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-2/docs/ADRs/0002-cycle2-scoped-fixes.md"},"output":"Read file /private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-2/docs/ADRs/0002-cycle2-scoped-fixes.md, lines 1-117\n1: # ADR 0002 — Cycle-2 scoped fixes: D-08 exception, analyzer honesty, CacheStore Phase-2, melos status\n2: \n3: - Status: accepted (items 2–4 record fact; item 1 is a conditional grant)\n4: - Date: 2026-10-29\n5: - Partition: p5 repo-hygiene-lows (Halloween TV)\n6: \n7: ## 1. D-08 ports-restructure exception (p4)\n8: \n9: ADR 0001 encodes design D-08 dependency-direction rules\n10: (contracts `<-` adapters; `core_*` never depends on `channel_*`,\n11: `infra_*`, or `kernel_app`). Partition p4\n12: (`orchestrator-cycle-2-part-p4-contracts-playlist-ports`) owns the\n13: contracts/playlist ports restructure.\n14: \n15: Fact (corrected at merged head): p4 **has landed** — commit `7e32d48`\n16: (`cycle-2 part p4-contracts-playlist-ports`), merge `72223a7`\n17: (`cycle-2 merge p4`). The \"no landed diff\" sentence above was true at the\n18: time of writing and is now superseded by this paragraph.\n19: \n20: Verified final p4 edge set (all point in the ADR 0001 direction; grant\n21: satisfied, no amendment needed):\n22: - `channel_api` -> `core_foundation` only;\n23: - `core_playlist` -> `core_foundation` only;\n24: - `core_cache` -> `core_foundation` + `core_playlist` only;\n25: - `core_effects` no longer -> `core_ui` (declared path dependency\n26:   removed; `core_ui` legitimately depends on `core_effects`);\n27: - `infra_firestore` / `infra_settings` -> `channel_api` (adapters consume\n28:   the contracts port; no `core_*`/`channel_*` edge points the wrong way).\n29: \n30: Decision — narrow conditional grant: p4 may relocate port\n31: declarations **among contract packages only**\n32: (`channel_api`, `core_cache`, `core_playlist`, `core_foundation`)\n33: without a new ADR, provided every resulting edge still points in\n34: the ADR 0001 direction. Any edge that would violate the direction\n35: rules (e.g. a `core_*` package depending on a `channel_*`,\n36: `infra_*`, or `kernel_app` package) requires an explicit amendment\n37: here **before** merge. Merge gate: the orchestrator confirms the\n38: final p4 edge set against ADR 0001 §Dependency-direction rules.\n39: \n40: ## 2. `dart analyze`, recorded honestly\n41: \n42: Environment: Flutter 3.47.7 / Dart 3.13.5 (stable), melos 6.3.3.\n43: \n44: - Fresh-checkout root `dart analyze`: **2810 issues**, dominated by\n45:   `uri_does_not_exist` / `undefined_identifier` cascades\n46:   (e.g. `package:flutter/material.dart` unresolvable). Cause: no\n47:   `.dart_tool/` exists in this worktree — per-package\n48:   `flutter pub get` never ran here. ADR 0001's \"No issues found!\"\n49:   is therefore **not reproducible from a fresh checkout**; it\n50:   assumed prior per-package resolution.\n51: - After `flutter pub get --offline` in each touched package,\n52:   `dart analyze packages/core_ui packages/core_effects\n53:   packages/testing_toolkit` reports **8 issues, all info-level\n54:   lints, zero errors/warnings**:\n55:   - `always_use_package_imports` ×4 (`cctv_tile.dart:6,7`,\n56:     `hud_overlay.dart:9`, `signal_lost.dart:6` — relative\n57:     `lib/` imports; pre-existing, outside this batch except the\n58:     `hud_overlay.dart` line, which is left as-is to keep the diff\n59:     minimal);\n60:   - `prefer_const_constructors` ×3 (`core_ui_test.dart:212,214,217`,\n61:     pre-existing);\n62:   - `prefer_final_locals` ×1 (`testing_toolkit.dart:43`,\n63:     pre-existing, file outside this partition).\n64: - Root `dart analyze` stays red until full-workspace resolution\n65:   exists — follow-up for whichever partition lands the root\n66:   pubspec (see §4).\n67: \n68: ## 3. Phase-2 full CacheStore adapter follow-up\n69: \n70: `FakeCacheStore` (`testing_toolkit`) is test-only and not a\n71: production cache:\n72: \n73: - `commit()` trusts the caller-supplied sha256 — it never hashes\n74:   `bytes`;\n75: - `deleteExpired()` clears **everything** and returns the count —\n76:   there is no TTL or expiry policy;\n77: - storage is a process-local `Map`, with no persistence.\n78: \n79: Phase-2 production adapter must: hash bytes on `commit` and\n80: reject mismatches, implement a real expiry policy, and persist\n81: `localRef`s. The `CacheStore` port signature in `core_cache`\n82: stays unchanged, so callers are unaffected.\n83: \n84: ## 4. melos status (probe, then revert)\n85: \n86: - Baseline: melos 6.3.3 refuses to run — `Found a melos.yaml file\n87:   ... but no local installation of Melos` (confirms ADR 0001).\n88: - Probe: added a temporary root `pubspec.yaml` (`name:\n89:   halloween_tv`, explicit `workspace:` list of all 14 members —\n90:   13 `packages/*` + `apps/tv_app` — plus `dev_dependencies:\n91:   melos: ^6.3.3`). `dart pub get --offline` fails with:\n92:   `packages/channel_api/pubspec.yaml is included in the workspace\n93:   from ./pubspec.yaml, but does not have 'resolution: workspace'.`\n94: - Conclusion: **not trivially viable**. Enabling workspaces needs\n95:   `resolution: workspace` in all 14 member pubspecs plus the root\n96:   pubspec — all outside the p5 file list — so the probe file was\n97:   deleted, `melos.yaml` is left untouched, and the `melos *`\n98:   scripts remain aspirational until the workspace owner lands the\n99:   root pubspec + member migrations.\n100: \n101: ## Verification (this partition)\n102: \n103: - `flutter pub get --offline` in `core_ui`, `core_effects`,\n104:   `testing_toolkit`: resolved (pub notes 2 packages with newer\n105:   incompatible versions; resolution itself succeeds).\n106: - `flutter test --no-pub` per package: core_ui 13 passed,\n107:   core_effects 15 passed, testing_toolkit 12 passed.\n108: - `git check-ignore -v apps/tv_app/.env` → ignored\n109:   (`apps/tv_app/.gitignore:46`); root `**/.env*` also covers it.\n110:   `.env.example` is explicitly re-included (`!**/.env.example`)\n111:   and shows as committable (`??`) in `git status`.\n112: - `.env.example` contains placeholder values only; zero secrets.\n113: - `core_effects` no longer declares the `core_ui` path dependency\n114:   (nothing under `packages/core_effects/lib` ever imported it;\n115:   this also removes the declared `core_effects` ↔ `core_ui`\n116:   dependency cycle, since `core_ui` legitimately depends on\n117:   `core_effects`).","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-2/docs/ADRs/0002-cycle2-scoped-fixes.md, lines 1-117\n1: # ADR 0002 — Cycle-2 scoped fixes: D-08 exception, analyzer honesty, CacheStore Phase-2, melos status\n2: \n3: - Status: accepted (items 2–4 record fact; item 1 is a conditional grant)\n4: - Date: 2026-10-29\n5: - Partition: p5 repo-hygiene-lows (Halloween TV)\n6: \n7: ## 1. D-08 ports-restructure exception (p4)\n8: \n9: ADR 0001 encodes design D-08 dependency-direction rules\n10: (contracts `<-` adapters; `core_*` never depends on `channel_*`,\n11: `infra_*`, or `kernel_app`). Partition p4\n12: (`orchestrator-cycle-2-part-p4-contracts-playlist-ports`) owns the\n13: contracts/playlist ports restructure.\n14: \n15: Fact (corrected at merged head): p4 **has landed** — commit `7e32d48`\n16: (`cycle-2 part p4-contracts-playlist-ports`), merge `72223a7`\n17: (`cycle-2 merge p4`). The \"no landed diff\" sentence above was true at the\n18: time of writing and is now superseded by this paragraph.\n19: \n20: Verified final p4 edge set (all point in the ADR 0001 direction; grant\n21: satisfied, no amendment needed):\n22: - `channel_api` -> `core_foundation` only;\n23: - `core_playlist` -> `core_foundation` only;\n24: - `core_cache` -> `core_foundation` + `core_playlist` only;\n25: - `core_effects` no longer -> `core_ui` (declared path dependency\n26:   removed; `core_ui` legitimately depends on `core_effects`);\n27: - `infra_firestore` / `infra_settings` -> `channel_api` (adapters consume\n28:   the contracts port; no `core_*`/`channel_*` edge points the wrong way).\n29: \n30: Decision — narrow conditional grant: p4 may relocate port\n31: declarations **among contract packages only**\n32: (`channel_api`, `core_cache`, `core_playlist`, `core_foundation`)\n33: without a new ADR, provided every resulting edge still points in\n34: the ADR 0001 direction. Any edge that would violate the direction\n35: rules (e.g. a `core_*` package depending on a `channel_*`,\n36: `infra_*`, or `kernel_app` package) requires an explicit amendment\n37: here **before** merge. Merge gate: the orchestrator confirms the\n38: final p4 edge set against ADR 0001 §Dependency-direction rules.\n39: \n40: ## 2. `dart analyze`, recorded honestly\n41: \n42: Environment: Flutter 3.47.7 / Dart 3.13.5 (stable), melos 6.3.3.\n43: \n44: - Fresh-checkout root `dart analyze`: **2810 issues**, dominated by\n45:   `uri_does_not_exist` / `undefined_identifier` cascades\n46:   (e.g. `package:flutter/material.dart` unresolvable). Cause: no\n47:   `.dart_tool/` exists in this worktree — per-package\n48:   `flutter pub get` never ran here. ADR 0001's \"No issues found!\"\n49:   is therefore **not reproducible from a fresh checkout**; it\n50:   assumed prior per-package resolution.\n51: - After `flutter pub get --offline` in each touched package,\n52:   `dart analyze packages/core_ui packages/core_effects\n53:   packages/testing_toolkit` reports **8 issues, all info-level\n54:   lints, zero errors/warnings**:\n55:   - `always_use_package_imports` ×4 (`cctv_tile.dart:6,7`,\n56:     `hud_overlay.dart:9`, `signal_lost.dart:6` — relative\n57:     `lib/` imports; pre-existing, outside this batch except the\n58:     `hud_overlay.dart` line, which is left as-is to keep the diff\n59:     minimal);\n60:   - `prefer_const_constructors` ×3 (`core_ui_test.dart:212,214,217`,\n61:     pre-existing);\n62:   - `prefer_final_locals` ×1 (`testing_toolkit.dart:43`,\n63:     pre-existing, file outside this partition).\n64: - Root `dart analyze` stays red until full-workspace resolution\n65:   exists — follow-up for whichever partition lands the root\n66:   pubspec (see §4).\n67: \n68: ## 3. Phase-2 full CacheStore adapter follow-up\n69: \n70: `FakeCacheStore` (`testing_toolkit`) is test-only and not a\n71: production cache:\n72: \n73: - `commit()` trusts the caller-supplied sha256 — it never hashes\n74:   `bytes`;\n75: - `deleteExpired()` clears **everything** and returns the count —\n76:   there is no TTL or expiry policy;\n77: - storage is a process-local `Map`, with no persistence.\n78: \n79: Phase-2 production adapter must: hash bytes on `commit` and\n80: reject mismatches, implement a real expiry policy, and persist\n81: `localRef`s. The `CacheStore` port signature in `core_cache`\n82: stays unchanged, so callers are unaffected.\n83: \n84: ## 4. melos status (probe, then revert)\n85: \n86: - Baseline: melos 6.3.3 refuses to run — `Found a melos.yaml file\n87:   ... but no local installation of Melos` (confirms ADR 0001).\n88: - Probe: added a temporary root `pubspec.yaml` (`name:\n89:   halloween_tv`, explicit `workspace:` list of all 14 members —\n90:   13 `packages/*` + `apps/tv_app` — plus `dev_dependencies:\n91:   melos: ^6.3.3`). `dart pub get --offline` fails with:\n92:   `packages/channel_api/pubspec.yaml is included in the workspace\n93:   from ./pubspec.yaml, but does not have 'resolution: workspace'.`\n94: - Conclusion: **not trivially viable**. Enabling workspaces needs\n95:   `resolution: workspace` in all 14 member pubspecs plus the root\n96:   pubspec — all outside the p5 file list — so the probe file was\n97:   deleted, `melos.yaml` is left untouched, and the `melos *`\n98:   scripts remain aspirational until the workspace owner lands the\n99:   root pubspec + member migrations.\n100: \n101: ## Verification (this partition)\n102: \n103: - `flutter pub get --offline` in `core_ui`, `core_effects`,\n104:   `testing_toolkit`: resolved (pub notes 2 packages with newer\n105:   incompatible versions; resolution itself succeeds).\n106: - `flutter test --no-pub` per package: core_ui 13 passed,\n107:   core_effects 15 passed, testing_toolkit 12 passed.\n108: - `git check-ignore -v apps/tv_app/.env` → ignored\n109:   (`apps/tv_app/.gitignore:46`); root `**/.env*` also covers it.\n110:   `.env.example` is explicitly re-included (`!**/.env.example`)\n111:   and shows as committable (`??`) in `git status`.\n112: - `.env.example` contains placeholder values only; zero secrets.\n113: - `core_effects` no longer declares the `core_ui` path dependency\n114:   (nothing under `packages/core_effects/lib` ever imported it;\n115:   this also removes the declared `core_effects` ↔ `core_ui`\n116:   dependency cycle, since `core_ui` legitimately depends on\n117:   `core_effects`)."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false,"state":{"itemId":"fc_01a192aab94c71ff90522306de3f5a1e"}},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-2/docs/ADRs/0002-cycle2-scoped-fixes.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793462024609,"end":1793462025147}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793462025149,"sessionID":"ses_e6d5a7eaaffeH1wroUP5Ck5Yd2","part":{"partID":"prt_192aab56c001IRwcQRwWqStA2W","sessionID":"ses_e6d5a7eaaffeH1wroUP5Ck5Yd2","messageID":"msg_192a62613001K0566H7d8ZL8Po","type":"tool","id":"call_01a192aab45a714db84a599e987876a0","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-2/apps/tv_app/lib/src/wall/live_wall_session.dart"},"output":"Read file /private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-2/apps/tv_app/lib/src/wall/live_wall_session.dart, lines 1-236\n1: /// Owns the live manifest subscription and staged activation lifecycle.\n2: library;\n3: \n4: import 'dart:async';\n5: import 'dart:convert';\n6: \n7: import 'package:core_playlist/core_playlist.dart';\n8: import 'package:kernel_app/kernel_app.dart';\n9: \n10: /// Watches control-plane observations after the verified offline wall is up.\n11: /// A candidate is emitted to playback only after all media is committed, ACK\n12: /// succeeds, and its real playback handle prepares and activates successfully.\n13: final class LiveWallSession {\n14:   LiveWallSession({\n15:     required this.partyId,\n16:     required this.channelId,\n17:     required ManifestSource<PlaybackManifest> manifestSource,\n18:     required PreparePlayback preparation,\n19:     CappedExponentialBackoff? backoff,\n20:   }) : _manifestSource = manifestSource,\n21:        _preparation = preparation,\n22:        _backoff = backoff ?? CappedExponentialBackoff();\n23: \n24:   final String partyId;\n25:   final String channelId;\n26:   final ManifestSource<PlaybackManifest> _manifestSource;\n27:   final PreparePlayback _preparation;\n28:   final CappedExponentialBackoff _backoff;\n29:   final StreamController<PlaybackSyncSnapshot> _updates =\n30:       StreamController<PlaybackSyncSnapshot>.broadcast();\n31: \n32:   StreamSubscription<PlaybackManifest>? _subscription;\n33:   Timer? _retryTimer;\n34:   PlaybackManifest? _pending;\n35:   PlaybackManifest? _retryManifest;\n36:   Future<void> Function(PlaybackSyncSnapshot)? _activate;\n37:   bool _started = false;\n38:   bool _processing = false;\n39:   bool _disposed = false;\n40:   bool _reconnect = false;\n41:   int _activationFailures = 0;\n42:   int _highestObservedVersion = 0;\n43:   String? _lastActivatedFingerprint;\n44:   String? _lastFailedFingerprint;\n45: \n46:   /// Complete versions successfully activated by the TV wall.\n47:   Stream<PlaybackSyncSnapshot> get changes => _updates.stream;\n48: \n49:   /// Starts observing after offline boot. [activate] performs actual wall\n50:   /// source preparation and activation through the app-owned handle.\n51:   void start({required Future<void> Function(PlaybackSyncSnapshot) activate}) {\n52:     if (_started || _disposed) return;\n53:     _started = true;\n54:     _activate = activate;\n55:     _listen();\n56:   }\n57: \n58:   void _listen() {\n59:     if (_disposed || _subscription != null) return;\n60:     try {\n61:       _subscription = _manifestSource\n62:           .watchCurrent(partyId: partyId, channelId: channelId)\n63:           .listen(\n64:             _observe,\n65:             onError: (Object error, StackTrace stack) => _sourceFailed(error),\n66:             onDone: _sourceClosed,\n67:             cancelOnError: true,\n68:           );\n69:     } on Object catch (error) {\n70:       _sourceFailed(error);\n71:     }\n72:   }\n73: \n74:   void _observe(PlaybackManifest manifest) {\n75:     if (_disposed ||\n76:         manifest.partyId != partyId ||\n77:         manifest.channelId != channelId) {\n78:       return;\n79:     }\n80:     final String fingerprint = _fingerprint(manifest);\n81:     if (manifest.version < _highestObservedVersion) return;\n82:     if (manifest.version > _highestObservedVersion) {\n83:       _highestObservedVersion = manifest.version;\n84:       if (_retryManifest != null &&\n85:           _retryManifest!.version < manifest.version) {\n86:         _retryManifest = null;\n87:       }\n88:     }\n89:     if (fingerprint == _lastActivatedFingerprint ||\n90:         fingerprint == _lastFailedFingerprint) {\n91:       return;\n92:     }\n93:     if (_pending != null && _pending!.version > manifest.version) return;\n94:     _pending = manifest;\n95:     _retryTimer?.cancel();\n96:     _retryTimer = null;\n97:     unawaited(_drain());\n98:   }\n99: \n100:   Future<void> _drain() async {\n101:     if (_processing || _disposed) return;\n102:     _processing = true;\n103:     try {\n104:       while (!_disposed && _pending != null) {\n105:         final PlaybackManifest manifest = _pending!;\n106:         _pending = null;\n107:         final String fingerprint = _fingerprint(manifest);\n108:         if (fingerprint == _lastActivatedFingerprint) continue;\n109: \n110:         final PlaybackSyncSnapshot staged = await _preparation.prepareManifest(\n111:           manifest,\n112:         );\n113:         if (_disposed) return;\n114:         if (staged.state == PlaybackSyncState.ready &&\n115:             staged.hasCompleteMedia &&\n116:             staged.manifest != null &&\n117:             _fingerprint(staged.manifest!) == fingerprint) {\n118:           try {\n119:             await _preparation.activate(\n120:               _SessionPlaybackHandle(\n121:                 prepareAction: () async {\n122:                   if (_disposed) throw StateError('live session was disposed');\n123:                 },\n124:                 activateAction: () async {\n125:                   if (_disposed) throw StateError('live session was disposed');\n126:                   await _activate?.call(staged);\n127:                 },\n128:               ),\n129:             );\n130:             if (_disposed) return;\n131:             final PlaybackSyncSnapshot active = _preparation.snapshot;\n132:             if (active.state == PlaybackSyncState.ready &&\n133:                 active.hasCompleteMedia &&\n134:                 active.manifest != null &&\n135:                 _fingerprint(active.manifest!) == fingerprint) {\n136:               _lastActivatedFingerprint = fingerprint;\n137:               _lastFailedFingerprint = null;\n138:               _activationFailures = 0;\n139:               if (!_updates.isClosed) _updates.add(active);\n140:               continue;\n141:             }\n142:           } on Object {\n143:             // Preparation owns the diagnostic state and retry delay.\n144:           }\n145:         }\n146: \n147:         final PlaybackSyncSnapshot outcome = _preparation.snapshot;\n148:         if (outcome.state == PlaybackSyncState.errorFatal) {\n149:           _lastFailedFingerprint = fingerprint;\n150:         } else if (outcome.error?.startsWith('playback activation failed:') ==\n151:             true) {\n152:           // Decoder failures are not delivery failures. WallScreen has already\n153:           // rolled changed tiles back; retrying the same version would churn\n154:           // those current decoders again without changing the input bytes.\n155:           _lastFailedFingerprint = fingerprint;\n156:         } else {\n157:           _retryManifest = manifest;\n158:           _activationFailures++;\n159:           _scheduleRetry(\n160:             outcome.retryAfter ?? _backoff.delayFor(_activationFailures),\n161:           );\n162:           if (!_updates.isClosed) _updates.add(outcome);\n163:         }\n164:       }\n165:     } finally {\n166:       _processing = false;\n167:       if (!_disposed && _pending != null) unawaited(_drain());\n168:     }\n169:   }\n170: \n171:   void _sourceFailed(Object error) {\n172:     if (_disposed) return;\n173:     _subscription = null;\n174:     _reconnect = true;\n175:     _scheduleRetry(_backoff.delayFor(++_activationFailures));\n176:   }\n177: \n178:   void _sourceClosed() {\n179:     if (_disposed) return;\n180:     _subscription = null;\n181:     _reconnect = true;\n182:     _scheduleRetry(_backoff.delayFor(++_activationFailures));\n18