{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793462233933,"sessionID":"ses_e6d5a7eaaffeH1wroUP5Ck5Yd2","part":{"partID":"prt_192adc79f001zrWo1E1vIzPbbC","sessionID":"ses_e6d5a7eaaffeH1wroUP5Ck5Yd2","messageID":"msg_192ab71b00011ZZK05K42kqsQs","type":"tool","id":"call_01a192adc744708189995056cde7a468","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"/// ChannelContext.settings keys honored by [HauntedSurveillancePlugin.build].\n///\n/// Wall configuration travels through the channel contract (not through\n/// plugin re-instantiation): the app publishes its live wall state here and\n/// [HauntedSurveillancePlugin.build] applies it. Constructor fields remain\n/// as defaults for direct use; settings win when present so the registry\n/// object and any app-side copy can never diverge on wall config.\nclass CctvWallSettingsKeys {\n  /// When `true`, drops effect overlays and glitch ticking.\n  static const String effectsDisabled = 'effectsDisabled';\n\n  /// Wall manifest version the app currently displays (diagnostics only).\n  static const String manifestVersion = 'manifestVersion';\n\n  /// Whether the host pads HUD content into the overscan-safe area.\n  static const String overscanSafe = 'overscanSafe';\n\n  /// Optional per-camera label overrides (`{cameraId: label}`).\n  static const String labels = 'labels';\n\n  /// Party-scoped display cap for the number of visible cameras.\n  ///\n  /// Encoding: the string `'1'`, `'2'`, or `'4'` (persisted through the\n  /// contracts-layer `SettingsPort` as a string, scoped by party id).\n  /// Absent, invalid, or unreadable values default to `'4'` (four cameras).\n  ///\n  /// This is a DISPLAY CAP only: `effectiveCount = min(configuredCount,\n  /// manifest clip count)`. Reduced layouts still prepare + ACK the complete\n  /// received manifest, and generation presets keep producing 4 clips. See\n  /// [cctvCameraCountFromSettings] and [cctvEffectiveCount].\n  static const String cameraCount = 'cameraCount';\n\n  /// Transient hero-zoom target: the camera id shown fullscreen, or absent\n  /// for the grid. Never persisted; validated against the active slots\n  /// (unknown ids are ignored). See [cctvHeroCameraIdFromSettings].\n  static const String heroCameraId = 'heroCameraId';\n}\n\n/// Animation duration for grid relayouts and hero zoom in/out.\n///\n/// Shared by the wall and its tests so intermediate hero geometry can be\n/// asserted deterministically (pump a fraction of this duration).\nconst Duration kWallLayoutDuration = Duration(milliseconds: 250);\n\n/// Key of the wall root (layout + hero geometry assertions).\nconst ValueKey<String> kCctvWallKey = ValueKey<String>('cctv-wall');\n\n/// Reads the configured camera display cap from [settings].\n///\n/// Accepts the documented string encoding (`'1'`/`'2'`/`'4'`, surrounding\n/// whitespace tolerated) and, defensively, a raw int. Anything absent,\n/// invalid, or unreadable (wrong type, unparsable, unsupported count such\n/// as `3`) defaults to [kDefaultCctvClipCount] (four cameras).\nint cctvCameraCountFromSettings(ChannelSettings settings) {\n  final Object? raw = settings.values[CctvWallSettingsKeys.cameraCount];\n  final int? parsed = switch (raw) {\n    String s => int.tryParse(s.trim()),\n    int n => n,\n    _ => null,\n  };\n  if (parsed == null || !isSupportedCctvClipCount(parsed)) {\n    return kDefaultCctvClipCount;\n  }\n  return parsed;\n}\n\n/// Reads the transient hero-zoom target from [settings].\n///\n/// Returns the camera id when a non-empty string is present, else null\n/// (grid). Membership in the active slot set is validated by the wall, not\n/// here, so unknown ids degrade to the grid instead of taking it down.\nString? cctvHeroCameraIdFromSettings(ChannelSettings settings) {\n  final Object? raw = settings.values[CctvWallSettingsKeys.heroCameraId];\n  if (raw is! String || raw.isEmpty) {\n    return null;\n  }\n  return raw;\n}\n\n/// Derives the number of tiles the wall renders.\n///\n/// `effectiveCount = min(configuredCount, manifestClipCount)`: the setting\n/// can only ever HIDE cameras, never invent them. Both inputs are sanitized\n/// to supported counts first (unsupported configured values fall back to\n/// [kDefaultCctvClipCount]; an unsupported manifest length falls back to the\n/// full slot map so per-slot defaults degrade instead of crashing). Because\n/// the supported counts `{1, 2, 4}` are closed under `min`, the result is\n/// always a supported count.\nint cctvEffectiveCount({\n  required int configuredCount,\n  required int manifestClipCount,\n}) {\n  final int configured = isSupportedCctvClipCount(configuredCount)\n      ? configuredCount\n      : kDefaultCctvClipCount;\n  final int manifest = isSupportedCctvClipCount(manifestClipCount)\n      ? manifestClipCount\n      : cctvSlots.length;\n  return configured < manifest ? configured : manifest;\n}","oldString":"/// ChannelContext.settings keys honored by [HauntedSurveillancePlugin.build].\n///\n/// Wall configuration travels through the channel contract (not through\n/// plugin re-instantiation): the app publishes its live wall state here and\n/// [HauntedSurveillancePlugin.build] applies it. Constructor fields remain\n/// as defaults for direct use; settings win when present so the registry\n/// object and any app-side copy can never diverge on wall config.\nclass CctvWallSettingsKeys {\n  /// When `true`, drops effect overlays and glitch ticking.\n  static const String effectsDisabled = 'effectsDisabled';\n\n  /// Wall manifest version the app currently displays (diagnostics only).\n  static const String manifestVersion = 'manifestVersion';\n\n  /// Whether the host pads HUD content into the overscan-safe area.\n  static const String overscanSafe = 'overscanSafe';\n\n  /// Optional per-camera label overrides (`{cameraId: label}`).\n  static const String labels = 'labels';\n}","path":"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-2/packages/channel_cctv/lib/src/plugin.dart"},"output":"Edited packages/channel_cctv/lib/src/plugin.dart (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"packages/channel_cctv/lib/src/plugin.dart","patch":"Index: packages/channel_cctv/lib/src/plugin.dart\n===================================================================\n--- packages/channel_cctv/lib/src/plugin.dart\n+++ packages/channel_cctv/lib/src/plugin.dart\n@@ -62,10 +62,90 @@\n   static const String overscanSafe = 'overscanSafe';\n \n   /// Optional per-camera label overrides (`{cameraId: label}`).\n   static const String labels = 'labels';\n+\n+  /// Party-scoped display cap for the number of visible cameras.\n+  ///\n+  /// Encoding: the string `'1'`, `'2'`, or `'4'` (persisted through the\n+  /// contracts-layer `SettingsPort` as a string, scoped by party id).\n+  /// Absent, invalid, or unreadable values default to `'4'` (four cameras).\n+  ///\n+  /// This is a DISPLAY CAP only: `effectiveCount = min(configuredCount,\n+  /// manifest clip count)`. Reduced layouts still prepare + ACK the complete\n+  /// received manifest, and generation presets keep producing 4 clips. See\n+  /// [cctvCameraCountFromSettings] and [cctvEffectiveCount].\n+  static const String cameraCount = 'cameraCount';\n+\n+  /// Transient hero-zoom target: the camera id shown fullscreen, or absent\n+  /// for the grid. Never persisted; validated against the active slots\n+  /// (unknown ids are ignored). See [cctvHeroCameraIdFromSettings].\n+  static const String heroCameraId = 'heroCameraId';\n }\n \n+/// Animation duration for grid relayouts and hero zoom in/out.\n+///\n+/// Shared by the wall and its tests so intermediate hero geometry can be\n+/// asserted deterministically (pump a fraction of this duration).\n+const Duration kWallLayoutDuration = Duration(milliseconds: 250);\n+\n+/// Key of the wall root (layout + hero geometry assertions).\n+const ValueKey<String> kCctvWallKey = ValueKey<String>('cctv-wall');\n+\n+/// Reads the configured camera display cap from [settings].\n+///\n+/// Accepts the documented string encoding (`'1'`/`'2'`/`'4'`, surrounding\n+/// whitespace tolerated) and, defensively, a raw int. Anything absent,\n+/// invalid, or unreadable (wrong type, unparsable, unsupported count such\n+/// as `3`) defaults to [kDefaultCctvClipCount] (four cameras).\n+int cctvCameraCountFromSettings(ChannelSettings settings) {\n+  final Object? raw = settings.values[CctvWallSettingsKeys.cameraCount];\n+  final int? parsed = switch (raw) {\n+    String s => int.tryParse(s.trim()),\n+    int n => n,\n+    _ => null,\n+  };\n+  if (parsed == null || !isSupportedCctvClipCount(parsed)) {\n+    return kDefaultCctvClipCount;\n+  }\n+  return parsed;\n+}\n+\n+/// Reads the transient hero-zoom target from [settings].\n+///\n+/// Returns the camera id when a non-empty string is present, else null\n+/// (grid). Membership in the active slot set is validated by the wall, not\n+/// here, so unknown ids degrade to the grid instead of taking it down.\n+String? cctvHeroCameraIdFromSettings(ChannelSettings settings) {\n+  final Object? raw = settings.values[CctvWallSettingsKeys.heroCameraId];\n+  if (raw is! String || raw.isEmpty) {\n+    return null;\n+  }\n+  return raw;\n+}\n+\n+/// Derives the number of tiles the wall renders.\n+///\n+/// `effectiveCount = min(configuredCount, manifestClipCount)`: the setting\n+/// can only ever HIDE cameras, never invent them. Both inputs are sanitized\n+/// to supported counts first (unsupported configured values fall back to\n+/// [kDefaultCctvClipCount]; an unsupported manifest length falls back to the\n+/// full slot map so per-slot defaults degrade instead of crashing). Because\n+/// the supported counts `{1, 2, 4}` are closed under `min`, the result is\n+/// always a supported count.\n+int cctvEffectiveCount({\n+  required int configuredCount,\n+  required int manifestClipCount,\n+}) {\n+  final int configured = isSupportedCctvClipCount(configuredCount)\n+      ? configuredCount\n+      : kDefaultCctvClipCount;\n+  final int manifest = isSupportedCctvClipCount(manifestClipCount)\n+      ? manifestClipCount\n+      : cctvSlots.length;\n+  return configured < manifest ? configured : manifest;\n+}\n+\n /// Reads per-camera label overrides from [settings].\n ///\n /// Accepts any `Map` shape (the settings map is untyped) and keeps only\n /// string-keyed, string-valued entries.\n","status":"modified","additions":80,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited packages/channel_cctv/lib/src/plugin.dart (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false,"state":{"itemId":"fc_01a192adc744708189995056cde7a468"}},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"/// ChannelContext.settings keys honored by [HauntedSurveillancePlugin.build].\\n///\\n/// Wall configuration travels through the channel contract (not through\\n/// plugin re-instantiation): the app publishes its live wall state here and\\n/// [HauntedSurveillancePlugin.build] applies it. Constructor fields remain\\n/// as defaults for direct use; settings win when present so the registry\\n/// object and any app-side copy can never diverge on wall config.\\nclass CctvWallSettingsKeys {\\n  /// When `true`, drops effect overlays and glitch ticking.\\n  static const String effectsDisabled = 'effectsDisabled';\\n\\n  /// Wall manifest version the app currently displays (diagnostics only).\\n  static const String manifestVersion = 'manifestVersion';\\n\\n  /// Whether the host pads HUD content into the overscan-safe area.\\n  static const String overscanSafe = 'overscanSafe';\\n\\n  /// Optional per-camera label overrides (`{cameraId: label}`).\\n  static const String labels = 'labels';\\n\\n  /// Party-scoped display cap for the number of visible cameras.\\n  ///\\n  /// Encoding: the string `'1'`, `'2'`, or `'4'` (persisted through the\\n  /// contracts-layer `SettingsPort` as a string, scoped by party id).\\n  /// Absent, invalid, or unreadable values default to `'4'` (four cameras).\\n  ///\\n  /// This is a DISPLAY CAP only: `effectiveCount = min(configuredCount,\\n  /// manifest clip count)`. Reduced layouts still prepare + ACK the complete\\n  /// received manifest, and generation presets keep producing 4 clips. See\\n  /// [cctvCameraCountFromSettings] and [cctvEffectiveCount].\\n  static const String cameraCount = 'cameraCount';\\n\\n  /// Transient hero-zoom target: the camera id shown fullscreen, or absent\\n  /// for the grid. Never persisted; validated against the active slots\\n  /// (unknown ids are ignored). See [cctvHeroCameraIdFromSettings].\\n  static const String heroCameraId = 'heroCameraId';\\n}\\n\\n/// Animation duration for grid relayouts and hero zoom in/out.\\n///\\n/// Shared by the wall and its tests so intermediate hero geometry can be\\n/// asserted deterministically (pump a fraction of this duration).\\nconst Duration kWallLayoutDuration = Duration(milliseconds: 250);\\n\\n/// Key of the wall root (layout + hero geometry assertions).\\nconst ValueKey<String> kCctvWallKey = ValueKey<String>('cctv-wall');\\n\\n/// Reads the configured camera display cap from [settings].\\n///\\n/// Accepts the documented string encoding (`'1'`/`'2'`/`'4'`, surrounding\\n/// whitespace tolerated) and, defensively, a raw int. Anything absent,\\n/// invalid, or unreadable (wrong type, unparsable, unsupported count such\\n/// as `3`) defaults to [kDefaultCctvClipCount] (four cameras).\\nint cctvCameraCountFromSettings(ChannelSettings settings) {\\n  final Object? raw = settings.values[CctvWallSettingsKeys.cameraCount];\\n  final int? parsed = switch (raw) {\\n    String s => int.tryParse(s.trim()),\\n    int n => n,\\n    _ => null,\\n  };\\n  if (parsed == null || !isSupportedCctvClipCount(parsed)) {\\n    return kDefaultCctvClipCount;\\n  }\\n  return parsed;\\n}\\n\\n/// Reads the transient hero-zoom target from [settings].\\n///\\n/// Returns the camera id when a non-empty string is present, else null\\n/// (grid). Membership in the active slot set is validated by the wall, not\\n/// here, so unknown ids degrade to the grid instead of taking it down.\\nString? cctvHeroCameraIdFromSettings(ChannelSettings settings) {\\n  final Object? raw = settings.values[CctvWallSettingsKeys.heroCameraId];\\n  if (raw is! String || raw.isEmpty) {\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n  return raw;\\n}\\n\\n/// Derives the number of tiles the wall renders.\\n///\\n/// `effectiveCount = min(configuredCount, manifestClipCount)`: the setting\\n/// can only ever HIDE cameras, never invent them. Both inputs are sanitized\\n/// to supported counts first (unsupported configured values fall back to\\n/// [kDefaultCctvClipCount]; an unsupported manifest length falls back to the\\n/// full slot map so per-slot defaults degrade instead of crashing). Because\\n/// the supported counts `{1, 2, 4}` are closed under `min`, the result is\\n/// always a supported count.\\nint cctvEffectiveCount({\\n  required int configuredCount,\\n  required int manifestClipCount,\\n}) {\\n  final int configured = isSupportedCctvClipCount(configuredCount)\\n      ? configuredCount\\n      : kDefaultCctvClipCount;\\n  final int manifest = isSupportedCctvClipCount(manifestClipCount)\\n      ? manifestClipCount\\n      : cctvSlots.length;\\n  return configured < manifest ? configured : manifest;\\n}\",\"oldString\":\"/// ChannelContext.settings keys honored by [HauntedSurveillancePlugin.build].\\n///\\n/// Wall configuration travels through the channel contract (not through\\n/// plugin re-instantiation): the app publishes its live wall state here and\\n/// [HauntedSurveillancePlugin.build] applies it. Constructor fields remain\\n/// as defaults for direct use; settings win when present so the registry\\n/// object and any app-side copy can never diverge on wall config.\\nclass CctvWallSettingsKeys {\\n  /// When `true`, drops effect overlays and glitch ticking.\\n  static const String effectsDisabled = 'effectsDisabled';\\n\\n  /// Wall manifest version the app currently displays (diagnostics only).\\n  static const String manifestVersion = 'manifestVersion';\\n\\n  /// Whether the host pads HUD content into the overscan-safe area.\\n  static const String overscanSafe = 'overscanSafe';\\n\\n  /// Optional per-camera label overrides (`{cameraId: label}`).\\n  static const String labels = 'labels';\\n}\",\"path\":\"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-2/packages/channel_cctv/lib/src/plugin.dart\"}"},"time":{"start":1793462224799,"end":1793462233933}}}}
