{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793462241150,"sessionID":"ses_e6d5a7eaaffeH1wroUP5Ck5Yd2","part":{"partID":"prt_192adf391001dV4gKPQVqTtxY3","sessionID":"ses_e6d5a7eaaffeH1wroUP5Ck5Yd2","messageID":"msg_192adeb9f001rc2Gx8R0ZcPx0v","type":"tool","id":"call_01a192adefe973abaa43ea5975903825","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"  @override\n  Widget build(ChannelContext context) {\n    // Wall config flows through the channel contract: settings published by\n    // the host win over constructor defaults, so the registry object never\n    // needs to be discarded/re-instantiated to change wall behaviour.\n    final bool settingsDisabled = context.settings\n        .get<bool>(CctvWallSettingsKeys.effectsDisabled, false);\n    // `cameraCount` follows the same rule (present settings win, absent\n    // settings keep the constructor default for direct use); the hero target\n    // is transient UI state that is never persisted, so a settings value\n    // wins when present and the constructor default applies otherwise.\n    final bool hasCountOverride = context.settings.values.containsKey(\n      CctvWallSettingsKeys.cameraCount,\n    );\n    return CctvWall(\n      playbackHandle: context.playbackHandle,\n      tileBuilder: tileBuilder,\n      profile: profile ??\n          (manifest == null\n              ? cctvProfile()\n              : effectProfileFromOverlay(manifest!.overlay)),\n      manifest: manifest,\n      clock: clock,\n      disableEffects: disableEffects || settingsDisabled,\n      glitchSeed: glitchSeed,\n      labelOverrides: cctvLabelOverridesFromSettings(context.settings),\n      cameraCount: hasCountOverride\n          ? cctvCameraCountFromSettings(context.settings)\n          : cameraCount,\n      heroCameraId:\n          cctvHeroCameraIdFromSettings(context.settings) ?? heroCameraId,\n    );\n  }\n}\n\n/// Adaptive CCTV wall shell (1, 2, or 4 cameras + decoder-preserving hero).\n///\n/// Boots by preparing the app-owned [PlaybackHandle], then shows one\n/// full-size tile, two side-by-side tiles in one row, or a 2x2 grid in\n/// canonical camera order, driven by [cameraCount] (display cap) and the\n/// received manifest (see [cctvEffectiveCount]). A single tile\n/// failure never takes down the wall: surface builders that throw are\n/// caught per tile and render [SignalLost].\n///\n/// Grid and hero geometry live in one full-viewport [Stack] with\n/// camera-keyed [AnimatedPositioned] children whose ancestry remains stable:\n/// opening the hero ([heroCameraId]) animates the selected existing tile to\n/// the viewport rectangle and fades its siblings (they stay mounted, so no\n/// decoder is created or disposed during the zoom). The host (app layer)\n/// owns focus and key handling; the wall only presents geometry.","oldString":"  @override\n  Widget build(ChannelContext context) {\n    // Wall config flows through the channel contract: settings published by\n    // the host win over constructor defaults, so the registry object never\n    // needs to be discarded/re-instantiated to change wall behaviour.\n    final bool settingsDisabled = context.settings\n        .get<bool>(CctvWallSettingsKeys.effectsDisabled, false);\n    return CctvWall(\n      playbackHandle: context.playbackHandle,\n      tileBuilder: tileBuilder,\n      profile: profile ??\n          (manifest == null\n              ? cctvProfile()\n              : effectProfileFromOverlay(manifest!.overlay)),\n      manifest: manifest,\n      clock: clock,\n      disableEffects: disableEffects || settingsDisabled,\n      glitchSeed: glitchSeed,\n      labelOverrides: cctvLabelOverridesFromSettings(context.settings),\n    );\n  }\n}\n\n/// 2x2 CCTV wall shell.\n///\n/// Boots by preparing the app-owned [PlaybackHandle], then shows four\n/// [CctvTile]s (video surface + HUD + effect overlay). A single tile\n/// failure never takes down the wall: surface builders that throw are\n/// caught per tile and render [SignalLost].","path":"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-2/packages/channel_cctv/lib/src/plugin.dart"},"output":"Edited packages/channel_cctv/lib/src/plugin.dart (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"packages/channel_cctv/lib/src/plugin.dart","patch":"Index: packages/channel_cctv/lib/src/plugin.dart\n===================================================================\n--- packages/channel_cctv/lib/src/plugin.dart\n+++ packages/channel_cctv/lib/src/plugin.dart\n@@ -228,8 +228,15 @@\n     // the host win over constructor defaults, so the registry object never\n     // needs to be discarded/re-instantiated to change wall behaviour.\n     final bool settingsDisabled = context.settings\n         .get<bool>(CctvWallSettingsKeys.effectsDisabled, false);\n+    // `cameraCount` follows the same rule (present settings win, absent\n+    // settings keep the constructor default for direct use); the hero target\n+    // is transient UI state that is never persisted, so a settings value\n+    // wins when present and the constructor default applies otherwise.\n+    final bool hasCountOverride = context.settings.values.containsKey(\n+      CctvWallSettingsKeys.cameraCount,\n+    );\n     return CctvWall(\n       playbackHandle: context.playbackHandle,\n       tileBuilder: tileBuilder,\n       profile: profile ??\n@@ -240,18 +247,32 @@\n       clock: clock,\n       disableEffects: disableEffects || settingsDisabled,\n       glitchSeed: glitchSeed,\n       labelOverrides: cctvLabelOverridesFromSettings(context.settings),\n+      cameraCount: hasCountOverride\n+          ? cctvCameraCountFromSettings(context.settings)\n+          : cameraCount,\n+      heroCameraId:\n+          cctvHeroCameraIdFromSettings(context.settings) ?? heroCameraId,\n     );\n   }\n }\n \n-/// 2x2 CCTV wall shell.\n+/// Adaptive CCTV wall shell (1, 2, or 4 cameras + decoder-preserving hero).\n ///\n-/// Boots by preparing the app-owned [PlaybackHandle], then shows four\n-/// [CctvTile]s (video surface + HUD + effect overlay). A single tile\n+/// Boots by preparing the app-owned [PlaybackHandle], then shows one\n+/// full-size tile, two side-by-side tiles in one row, or a 2x2 grid in\n+/// canonical camera order, driven by [cameraCount] (display cap) and the\n+/// received manifest (see [cctvEffectiveCount]). A single tile\n /// failure never takes down the wall: surface builders that throw are\n /// caught per tile and render [SignalLost].\n+///\n+/// Grid and hero geometry live in one full-viewport [Stack] with\n+/// camera-keyed [AnimatedPositioned] children whose ancestry remains stable:\n+/// opening the hero ([heroCameraId]) animates the selected existing tile to\n+/// the viewport rectangle and fades its siblings (they stay mounted, so no\n+/// decoder is created or disposed during the zoom). The host (app layer)\n+/// owns focus and key handling; the wall only presents geometry.\n class CctvWall extends StatefulWidget {\n   /// Creates the wall shell.\n   CctvWall({\n     super.key,\n","status":"modified","additions":24,"deletions":3}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited packages/channel_cctv/lib/src/plugin.dart (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false,"state":{"itemId":"fc_01a192adefe973abaa43ea5975903825"}},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"  @override\\n  Widget build(ChannelContext context) {\\n    // Wall config flows through the channel contract: settings published by\\n    // the host win over constructor defaults, so the registry object never\\n    // needs to be discarded/re-instantiated to change wall behaviour.\\n    final bool settingsDisabled = context.settings\\n        .get<bool>(CctvWallSettingsKeys.effectsDisabled, false);\\n    // `cameraCount` follows the same rule (present settings win, absent\\n    // settings keep the constructor default for direct use); the hero target\\n    // is transient UI state that is never persisted, so a settings value\\n    // wins when present and the constructor default applies otherwise.\\n    final bool hasCountOverride = context.settings.values.containsKey(\\n      CctvWallSettingsKeys.cameraCount,\\n    );\\n    return CctvWall(\\n      playbackHandle: context.playbackHandle,\\n      tileBuilder: tileBuilder,\\n      profile: profile ??\\n          (manifest == null\\n              ? cctvProfile()\\n              : effectProfileFromOverlay(manifest!.overlay)),\\n      manifest: manifest,\\n      clock: clock,\\n      disableEffects: disableEffects || settingsDisabled,\\n      glitchSeed: glitchSeed,\\n      labelOverrides: cctvLabelOverridesFromSettings(context.settings),\\n      cameraCount: hasCountOverride\\n          ? cctvCameraCountFromSettings(context.settings)\\n          : cameraCount,\\n      heroCameraId:\\n          cctvHeroCameraIdFromSettings(context.settings) ?? heroCameraId,\\n    );\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/// Adaptive CCTV wall shell (1, 2, or 4 cameras + decoder-preserving hero).\\n///\\n/// Boots by preparing the app-owned [PlaybackHandle], then shows one\\n/// full-size tile, two side-by-side tiles in one row, or a 2x2 grid in\\n/// canonical camera order, driven by [cameraCount] (display cap) and the\\n/// received manifest (see [cctvEffectiveCount]). A single tile\\n/// failure never takes down the wall: surface builders that throw are\\n/// caught per tile and render [SignalLost].\\n///\\n/// Grid and hero geometry live in one full-viewport [Stack] with\\n/// camera-keyed [AnimatedPositioned] children whose ancestry remains stable:\\n/// opening the hero ([heroCameraId]) animates the selected existing tile to\\n/// the viewport rectangle and fades its siblings (they stay mounted, so no\\n/// decoder is created or disposed during the zoom). The host (app layer)\\n/// owns focus and key handling; the wall only presents geometry.\",\"oldString\":\"  @override\\n  Widget build(ChannelContext context) {\\n    // Wall config flows through the channel contract: settings published by\\n    // the host win over constructor defaults, so the registry object never\\n    // needs to be discarded/re-instantiated to change wall behaviour.\\n    final bool settingsDisabled = context.settings\\n        .get<bool>(CctvWallSettingsKeys.effectsDisabled, false);\\n    return CctvWall(\\n      playbackHandle: context.playbackHandle,\\n      tileBuilder: tileBuilder,\\n      profile: profile ??\\n          (manifest == null\\n              ? cctvProfile()\\n              : effectProfileFromOverlay(manifest!.overlay)),\\n      manifest: manifest,\\n      clock: clock,\\n      disableEffects: disableEffects || settingsDisabled,\\n      glitchSeed: glitchSeed,\\n      labelOverrides: cctvLabelOverridesFromSettings(context.settings),\\n    );\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/// 2x2 CCTV wall shell.\\n///\\n/// Boots by preparing the app-owned [PlaybackHandle], then shows four\\n/// [CctvTile]s (video surface + HUD + effect overlay). A single tile\\n/// failure never takes down the wall: surface builders that throw are\\n/// caught per tile and render [SignalLost].\",\"path\":\"/private/tmp/orchestrator/cycle-12/part-2/packages/channel_cctv/lib/src/plugin.dart\"}"},"time":{"start":1793462236049,"end":1793462241150}}}}
